  {"id":166,"x":-580,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws."],"exits":[{"to":163,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":165,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":167,"x":-600,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws."],"exits":[{"to":164,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":168,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":168,"x":-600,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws.","Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws.  A peculiar stone wall can barely be seen above the tall grass."],"exits":[{"to":167,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":161,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":169,"x":-620,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws."],"exits":[{"to":170,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":165,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":207,"exit":"go","move":"go willow trees"}]},
  {"id":170,"x":-620,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws."],"exits":[{"to":169,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":171,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":171,"x":-640,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["Grass, once of a type used for food but now grown wild, rises above a tall human's head.  Your view here is limited to a few feet in any direction and it would be easy to become lost.  Claw marks in the gritty soil show that others have been here before you.  Perhaps they await you, lying silent in the grass waiting for you to blunder into their jaws."],"exits":[{"to":170,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":172,"exit":"go","move":"go small clearing"}]},
  {"id":172,"x":-640,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Grasslands","descriptions":["You stand surrounded on all sides by high grass that blocks the view after more than a few feet.  The tall stalks rustle softly, stirred by unfelt breezes, or worse.  Your shoulders twitch as if momentarily expecting to feel the hot breath of some unseen predator upon them.  There seems no clear choice of direction out of this grassy trap."],"exits":[{"to":171,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":173,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow hole"}]},
  {"id":173,"x":-620,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["Daylight, achingly bright here in the darkness of this tunnel, fails to penetrate very far down into the cool, slimy depths.  Hard-packed dirt walls form a steep funnel sloping down from a ruined farm wagon overhead into the unknown.  The whole place reminds you disturbingly of the traps some insects dig in the sand to ensnare other insects passing by.  From far down the tunnel, a faint clicking sound emanates."],"exits":[{"to":174,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":172,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow hole"}]},
  {"id":174,"x":-600,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["To the northwest, there is a faint breath of fresh air.  Southeast, deeper into the darkness, faint clicking noises and a barely heard whirring sound like the rustle of dry leaves can be made out.  The walls are smooth and slightly slimy to the touch.  Your breath catches in your throat from the odd musty smell mingled with the stink of rotting organic matter."],"exits":[{"to":175,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":173,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":175,"x":-580,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["Darkness all about you hinders your senses and confuses your notions of direction.  Something thick and glutinous turns under your foot with a disgusting squelch and you taste bile in the back of your throat.  A clicking noise as of dry sticks hitting each other overlays a subdued rustling sound.  The air is thick with the sweet, sickly smell of festering meat."],"exits":[{"to":176,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":174,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":176,"x":-560,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["A tiny flicker of pale green light here and there from loathsome misshapen fungi on the walls gives you barely enough light to see your hands in front of you.  The walls and low roof overhead drip with a thick and sticky secretion that clings to you coldly.  Something pale and bulbous crunches under a careless step, and a fine white mist squirts into the air from the ruined thing.  The stench of rotting flesh is overpowering."],"exits":[{"to":177,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":175,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":177,"x":-540,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["Clicking and rustling noises loom large in your ears as your eyes grasp vainly in the uncertain fungal glow for the source of the noise.  Mucous-like goo drips in an almost continual rain from overhead and fouls the walls and floor with its viscous mess.  Something dark and very fast scuttles by, its hard carapace brushing against you in the gloom.  The clicking dies away a moment and then returns, now with a sinister overtone of urgency to it."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":176,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":178,"x":-520,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnels","descriptions":["In the faint glow of huge fungi on the befouled walls, you can see that here a tunnel widens out into a wedge-shaped room.  The walls glisten with a thick layer of slime and trails of it cross the floor like half-jelled mud.  Your eyes seem to think they catch movement in the corners of your vision, but when you look directly, you see only rock and dirt and muck."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":179,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":177,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":179,"x":-520,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["The walls here grow thick with putrid-smelling fungi that gleam with a foul internal light.  For what the light reveals, you'd rather they not be here at all.  From a rounded roof hang dozens of bloated monsters.  Looking like enormous, pulsating sacks of flesh, they have vaguely insect-like heads with massive jaws that dig deep into the roof to hold them in place.  Enormous, distended guts pulsate slowly and through the thin chitin, you can make out faint shapes moving in some thick ooze."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":180,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":180,"x":-520,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["The air here is so heavy with the stench of rotting matter that you gasp for breath in the foul miasma.  The floor is hip-deep in decaying refuse and here and there, a gleaming bone pokes up out of the pulsating mass.  Dark insectile shapes scuttle about, on and in thick porridge of rot, seemingly oblivious to your presence.  You watch one for a moment, to your regret, as it voids half a gill or more of noisome semi-liquid from its maw into the mess and scuttles off."],"exits":[{"to":179,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":181,"x":-500,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["The floor is of loose rock and mud, mixed with the endless slime that drools in long strands from every surface.  Your footing is treacherous and uncertain.  The thought of falling into the unwholesome muck that is the floor makes you retch sour vomit.  Dark shapes scuttle about, moving in and out among the stones and rubble but never quite there when you look directly at them.  The air is thick and a loud clicking fills your ears.  Something cold and wet drips stickily down the back of your neck."],"exits":[{"to":182,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":178,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":182,"x":-500,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["The room is thick with danger.  You feel dozens of cold, unblinking eyes watching your every move.  Heavy strands of viscous slime trail from the roof and walls, making your footing uncertain and causing you to shy away from their clinging touch.  An enormous toadstool, thick and tall as a Dwarf, glimmers with an evil yellow glow casting strange shadows all about.  With an increasing sense of fear, you realize the shadows are moving towards you."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":183,"exit":"go","move":"go slime-choked passage"},{"to":184,"exit":"none","move":"room -rub enormous toadstool;-1get pale spores;-throw my pale spores at curtain slime;-1go curtain slime"}]},
  {"id":183,"x":-500,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["This huge, hemispherical chamber is a nightmare of wriggling movement and unclean shapes.  Rows of rough cylinders, apparently made of festering matter laced with the ever-present slime, pulsate from within in a grotesque manner.  Mud-colored insectile shapes crawl around and over them, apparently tending them and keeping them moist.  At the far end of the chamber, a latticework of dried slime and mud shields something enormous and foul from your full sight, but not you from its.","This huge, hemispherical chamber is a nightmare of wriggling movement and unclean shapes.  Rows of rough cylinders, apparently made of festering matter laced with the ever-present slime, pulsate from within in a grotesque manner.  Mud-colored insectile shapes crawl around and over them, apparently tending them and keeping them moist.  At the far end of the chamber, a latticework of dried slime and mud hides something enormous and foul from full sight."],"exits":[{"to":182,"exit":"go","move":"go slime-choked passage"}]},
  {"id":184,"x":-480,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["This wedge-shaped chamber narrows down to a tunnel that passes to the southeast.  The air here is heavy with a foul stench of rotting matter and heavy ropes of thick mucous-like slime cover every surface.","This wedge-shaped chamber narrows down to a tunnel that passes to the southeast.  The air here is heavy with a foul stench of rotting matter and heavy ropes of thick mucous-like slime cover every surface.  An enormous toadstool, thick and tall as a Dwarf, glimmers with an evil yellow glow casting strange shadows all about."],"exits":[{"to":185,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":182,"exit":"none","move":"room -rub enormous toadstool;-1get pale spores;-throw my pale spores at curtain slime;-1go curtain slime"}]},
  {"id":185,"x":-460,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["Curving tunnel walls here are thick with a mucous-like substance that sticks to your hands and feet and equipment.  Heavy odors of rot and corruption invade your nostrils and make you gag.  Loud rustling sounds fill your ears.  Among the stinks and foulness, a tiny hint of fresher air drifts from the southeast."],"exits":[{"to":186,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":184,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":186,"x":-440,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["The tunnel walls are covered with a sticky, drying, mass of slime.  Small, scabrous-looking mushrooms encrust the rocks here and there and gleam with a faint light.  You can barely make out the deeper blackness ahead and behind you.  The air stings your throat with a smell composed of rotting matter and refuse that makes the worst of the slums you have walked seem like gardens of roses in your memory."],"exits":[{"to":187,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":185,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":187,"x":-420,"y":360,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Tunnel","descriptions":["From far to the northwest, a faint and ominous clicking sound can be heard.  The walls here are slimy and sticky, making them unpleasant to touch.  Tiny lumps of glowing toadstools along the floor keep you from totally losing your sense of perspective and direction."],"exits":[{"to":188,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":186,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":188,"x":-400,"y":380,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Underground Chamber","descriptions":["The space here is somewhat larger than a tunnel but only by a fraction.  To the northwest, deeper blackness shows a path.  Overhead, the roof seems to be startlingly regular and not made of the congealed slime and mud that can be faintly seen upon the walls.  Several large, square stones have fallen to the floor from overhead leaving a gaping dark hole."],"exits":[{"to":187,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":189,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stones"}]},
  {"id":189,"x":-360,"y":360,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Grand Hall","descriptions":["This huge room was the banqueting and festive hall for the manor in happier days.  Long trestle tables, now ruined and wrecked, once lined the great hall facing a raised dais for the lord and his noble guests at the far end.  Broken windows have let in rain and wind and the room is fetid with mold and rotfungus.  Once elegant wallpaper now dangles in forlorn tatters from the high walls.  A curious mound squats in one dark corner and from it there seems a trail worn in the muck on the floor."],"exits":[{"to":192,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":190,"exit":"go","move":"go kitchen door"},{"to":194,"exit":"go","move":"go double doors"},{"to":188,"exit":"go","move":"go curious mound"}],"aliases":["Manor House"]},
  {"id":190,"x":-340,"y":360,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Kitchen","descriptions":["Here is where feasts were prepared and the trophies of the hunt were cleaned and dressed for cooking.  Marble-topped tables still stand but most of the wooden fittings are gone leaving only bits and splinters.  A huge fireplace takes up the far end of the room.  Hung alongside it are a few corroded pots, skewers and less-identifiable artifacts.  To the north is the pantry and buttery."],"exits":[{"to":191,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":189,"exit":"go","move":"go kitchen door"}]},
  {"id":191,"x":-340,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Pantry","descriptions":["This room has been almost completely gutted.  Only some brass fittings and hinges that once adorned the wooden cupboards remain.  Bits of wood, half-chewed and splintered, litter the floor.  Several stone tables and benches yet remain as well as some deep sinks used for food preparation.  Dried trails of slime criss-cross the floor and some even climb the walls."],"exits":[{"to":190,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":224,"exit":"go","move":"go rectangular trapdoor"}]},
  {"id":192,"x":-380,"y":360,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House, Trophy Room","descriptions":["This room once boasted a fine collection of mementoes of the hunt.  A few mounted heads yet remain on the walls.  Fierce creatures, some of which you have never beheld or even heard of, can still be seen here.  A massive cabinet that once held many curious and unusual weapons is now broken and empty.  One item still stands out, a small table, topped with a single gigantic scale.  You have no idea what it once adorned, but your respect for whoever hunted it rises."],"exits":[{"to":193,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":189,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"aliases":["Trophy Room"]},
  {"id":193,"x":-380,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Armory","descriptions":["This room was once used for weapon storage and maintenance.  Partly a museum and partly a workshop, racks and hooks for swords and spears line the walls and a small forge and anvil command the room's middle.  A broken boar-spear still lies in one corner, with dried blood on the blade."],"exits":[{"to":192,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":194,"x":-360,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Lodge Entry","descriptions":["Dark polished wood gleams dully in the subdued light of the entry hall of the manor.  Black and white tiles form a diamond pattern on the floor, reflecting the elegant taste of a bygone time.  Giant racks of antlers and mounted heads of snarling beasts line both walls.  A moth-eaten and ruined rug that was once the skin of some massive beast is crumpled up in one corner."],"exits":[{"to":195,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":196,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":198,"exit":"go","move":"go grand staircase"},{"to":189,"exit":"go","move":"go double doors"}]},
  {"id":195,"x":-340,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Lodge Library","descriptions":["This was once the library of the house.  Long ago stripped of any valuables either by the owner or by later thieves, the room is bare and cold.  The tall windows are smashed and broken and choked with crawling vines that have snaked their way in along the frames.  The wooden shelves have been used for firewood as evidenced by the ash on the floor and the soot on the ceiling.  The desiccated corpse of some forest dweller is sprawled across a blood-stained and burnt rug in the middle of the room."],"exits":[{"to":194,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":196,"x":-380,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Den","descriptions":["This small and intimate room was reserved for the lord of the manor and his close friends.  Rotting leather furniture and cobwebbed souvenirs of the hunt line the walls and focus on a large fireplace with a carved stone mantel.  Faded tapestries depicting people riding to hounds and pursuing stags and other scenes of blood-sport hang on the blotched and mildewed plaster walls.  Something once made a nest out of the stuffing in one of the couches and bits of fluff drift all over the room."],"exits":[{"to":194,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":197,"exit":"go","move":"go swinging doors"}]},
  {"id":197,"x":-400,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Billiard Room","descriptions":["The remains of a large billiard table are scattered about this spacious chamber.  Tatters of green felt litter the floor and several cue sticks lie splintered here and there.  One wall still holds a dart board though the darts imbedded have become rusty and useless.  A silver and crystal chandelier that once hung above the table seems to have survived the disaster, looking almost incongruous now in its dusty splendor."],"exits":[{"to":196,"exit":"go","move":"go swinging doors"}],"aliases":["Billiard Room"]},
  {"id":198,"x":-360,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Upper Hall","descriptions":["A wide balustraded corridor runs around three sides of the upper hall.  Faded carpet still depicts a scene of dozens of fantastic animals being hunted in various ways.  Widely spaced doors hint at the luxurious size of the rooms on this level."],"exits":[{"to":199,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":204,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":194,"exit":"go","move":"go grand staircase"}]},
  {"id":199,"x":-340,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Upper Hall","descriptions":["Near a set of grand stairs, the hallway seems in good shape.  Several doors remain in place, closing off unknown upper rooms.  The preserved head of a huge wild boar has broken loose from its wall hanging and dangles over the railing like an over-indulgent party-goer being ill."],"exits":[{"to":200,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":198,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":222,"exit":"go","move":"go solid door"}]},
  {"id":200,"x":-340,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Upper Hall East","descriptions":["This would appear to lead to the master suite of the lord of this house.  A huge door, solid and well made, still stands in silent guard over this ruined domain.  An elaborate coat of arms has been woven into the carpeting here and the colors remain fairly bright and unsullied."],"exits":[{"to":199,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":201,"exit":"go","move":"go massive door"}]},
  {"id":201,"x":-320,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House, Master Suite","descriptions":["This was a sitting room once.  Outfitted in an antique and elaborate style, the walls are hung with intricate tapestries and decorative moldings that still retain their heavy gilding.  Little furniture remains now and the fireplace shows where much of it ended up, to judge from the bits of gilded brass that were once handles and knobs and such among the ashes."],"exits":[{"to":202,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":200,"exit":"go","move":"go massive door"}]},
  {"id":202,"x":-320,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House, Master Bedroom","descriptions":["A huge canopied bed dominates this large room.  Obviously the sleeping chambers for the Lord of this place, the decor reflects the hunting themes so common throughout the building.  To one side, a massive desk made of polished bones surfaced with ivory holds a jumble of papers."],"exits":[{"to":203,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":201,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":203,"x":-320,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House, Upper Library","descriptions":["Rows of leather-bound books and pigeonholed racks of scrolls indicate the private library of the manor.  Time has been kind here and the place is surprisingly intact.  Whatever horror occured here long-ago, those involved could not bring themselves to burn or harm these ranked volumes.  Your eye is caught by something bizarre in this almost normal scene: in one large chair, a shrivelled corpse grins out at you eerily.  A blood-stained book still clutched in its gnarled hands."],"exits":[{"to":202,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":204,"x":-380,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Upper Hall","descriptions":["The hallway here is still relatively intact.  The walls retain a hint of the once-bright colors with which they were decorated.  A leak in the roof overhead has created numerous water-spots in the carpeting and allowed a unique collection of molds to spring up.  One or two of them look almost worthy of attention by the hunters depicted in the undamaged portions of the carpet."],"exits":[{"to":205,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":198,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":206,"exit":"go","move":"go wood door"},{"to":223,"exit":"go","move":"go white door"}]},
  {"id":205,"x":-380,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Upper Hall West","descriptions":["This end of the hallway is a ruin of collapsed plaster and stonework.  Anything left here has been buried under piles of rubble and dust that have been turned into a form of cement by rain and frost."],"exits":[{"to":204,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":206,"x":-400,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Bedroom","descriptions":["One of a number of rooms set aside for guests, this one has been thoroughly ransacked and looted.  A cracked stone basin and part of the iron bedstead are all that remain in here."],"exits":[{"to":204,"exit":"go","move":"go solid door"}]},
  {"id":207,"x":-640,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["To the north, tall overgrown grassland blocks your view.  South, a line of willow trees, foliage long and dangling, obscures anything in that direction.  The high growth on all sides cuts off any hint of breeze and the air is thick and humid.  Clouds of gnats swarm and dart all about and their low drone washes over you, numbing your senses.  The ground squishes underfoot, dragging at your feet and making your footing uncertain."],"exits":[{"to":208,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":209,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":210,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":169,"exit":"go","move":"go tall grassland"}]},
  {"id":208,"x":-620,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["A minor clearing sits here, surrounded by thick-set willows in a strangely circular clearing.  The stump of a long-dead and decayed tree rises high in the center of the clearing.  A grandfather of willow trees to judge from the thickness of the stump that remains.  A strange mold covers the ground here and every step sends small puffs of spores into the air.  Only the damp air keeps them from swirling high enough to be a threat to eyes or nose."],"exits":[{"to":211,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":209,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":207,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":209,"x":-640,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["Willow trees grow thick on all sides of you.  Long green fronds trail to the ground, still and lifeless in the heavy air.  Massive, gnarled tree trunks covered with dangling beards of moss look like old men hunched together in ragged cloaks.  To the south, the trees grow even taller, their heavy foliage casting a deep gloom over the fern-shrouded, damp ground."],"exits":[{"to":207,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":208,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":211,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":210,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Willow Tree Marsh"]},
  {"id":210,"x":-660,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["Thick fungi grow at odd angles from the gnarled brown trunks of the numerous willows growing all about.  A damp musty smell catches at your throat and stings your eyes.  A curious object, shaped like a dog-sized insect, lies tangled in thick fibrous strands of fungal material at the base of one tree.  A trail of large black ants troops up to the corpse in an unending line as nature quietly reclaims its dead."],"exits":[{"to":207,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":209,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":211,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":211,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":211,"x":-640,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["Great clumps of horsetail ferns sprout among the willows here.  The trees are thinner and more widely spaced, though they still grow close enough and thick enough to block your view after only a few feet.  Somewhere nearby, frogs croak in an irregular chorus.  Among the ferns, a lone bird calls, the sound echoing dully in the wet air."],"exits":[{"to":209,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":208,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":212,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":212,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":213,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":210,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":212,"x":-640,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["Heavy mud grabs at your feet and every movement results in loud squelching noises.  To the north, a thick line of willows stands a silent watch over this seeping marshland.  Clumps of ferns grow on small outcrops of drier land.  The rest is a sea of heavy mud and thick swamp-grass.  Southward, the land rises a bit and willows return to overgrow the marshes."],"exits":[{"to":211,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":213,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":213,"x":-660,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["A large patch of relatively dry ground sticks out from a grove of willows to the north.  Here and there, shallow pools of water glisten darkly through a heavy covering of marshflowers that cover their surface.  Hordes of bloodsucking insects throng around you, climbing into your eyes and nose and flying about your ears, their thin, high whining sound grating on your nerves.  To the south, the land continues its slow decline into the marshy bottomlands."],"exits":[{"to":212,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":214,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":214,"x":-660,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["Scattered willow trees cover this rise in the damp landscape.  Marshland flows both north and south like a heavy sea around a low island and even here, the earth is damp enough to squish as you move.  Frogs in all directions sing a raucous chorus in a curious harmony of high and low voices and somewhere a bird calls out in a long, lonely cry."],"exits":[{"to":213,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":219,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":217,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":216,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":215,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":218,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":215,"x":-680,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["A thin margin of fen runs down to a muddy riverbank.  South of that, a small river flows sluggishly, the current checked by tremendous growths of a drab-green water-weed that has formed thick mats across the stream.  An occasional fish breaks the soupy water to snatch at the unending clouds of midges and water-dancers that swarm above the stream."],"exits":[{"to":214,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":216,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":216,"x":-660,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["Stagnant water splashes about your feet as you tread carefully on the slippery mud.  A rough path wanders along a marshy strand between a line of willows and the sluggish river that blocks any progress southward.  Slime-worms ooze their gelid way through the thick ooze at your feet as something with a shiny carapace and numerous legs springs out of the ooze to grab one of them and drag it, struggling weakly, back beneath the thin film of water on the mud."],"exits":[{"to":214,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":217,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":215,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":217,"x":-640,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["A giant among willows has collapsed here, its foundation undermined by the seeping marsh as it spreads across the once-dry land.  Roots pulled free as the tree toppled now stand naked in the air as the dead giant slowly melts into the mud and decay.  A thick lacing of moss and less identifiable growths have sprung up along the trunk and branches where half a hundred spider webs gleam with collected dew among the still-green leaves."],"exits":[{"to":216,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":214,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":218,"x":-680,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["The land rises to the north where a line of massive willows sweeps the ground with their deep green fronds.  As the land drops to the south, it becomes damp and marshy.  Thick hummocks of drier ground hold clumps of tiny wild-flowers, giving a curiously lovely splash of color to the drab grey and brown of the scum-covered pools between them.  A sea of mud to the south fades indistinctly into a sluggish brown river."],"exits":[{"to":213,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":214,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":219,"x":-640,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Tree Marsh","descriptions":["A thin clump of willows grows on a relatively dry patch of higher ground surrounded by marshland.  Heavy clumps of rushes grow around the edge of the dry land and somewhere among them something is moving carefully.  A wading bird perhaps, in search of the numerous frogs who continually sound their varied notes on all sides."],"exits":[{"to":214,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":220,"x":-20,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Northwall Trail, Wooded Grove","descriptions":["A rhythmic chittering amid feathery patches of fern welcomes you to this grove.  Tall wyndwood and oak trees, thickly cloaked in ivy, arch over a thin trail that bends around the town wall to the northeast.  Like a puppeteer, the leafy canopy directs a dance of sunlight and shadow across the ground.","The rhythmic song of cicadas hums through the grove, welcoming the passerby's footfalls.  The silvery eyes of night peer down through the rustling canopy overhead, illuminating the bare soil of a thin trail that bends around the town wall to the northeast."],"exits":[{"to":221,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":1,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":265,"exit":"climb","move":"climb town wall"}]},
  {"id":221,"x":20,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Northwall Trail, Wooded Grove","descriptions":["The sweet smell of wildflowers carried on the breeze mingles with the spicy smell of cedar and juniper.  Sunlight dapples the mossy ground in golden hues and glistens on the dew-laden petals of tiny snowflowers.  A gnarled oak tree, cracked in two by a great tempest's fury, lays beside the trail.","The sweet smell of wildflowers carried on the breeze mingles with the spicy scent of cedar and juniper.  At the sound of an owl, a startled woodmouse scurries across the trail toward a gnarled and broken oak tree."],"exits":[{"to":264,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":220,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":265,"exit":"climb","move":"climb town wall"}]},
  {"id":222,"x":-340,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Bedroom","descriptions":["This room is fitted out as a guest bedroom for overnight visitors.  The bedding has long since rotted away leaving only the iron frame and some leather scraps that once formed the supports for the mattress.  Scraps of cloth and bits of discolored ribbon show that perhaps a lady once dwelt here.  A patch of blood-stained plaster on one wall shows you she did not enjoy her stay."],"exits":[{"to":199,"exit":"go","move":"go solid door"}]},
  {"id":223,"x":-380,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Linen Closet","descriptions":["A small storage area and workroom, this once held the supplies of linen such as sheets, blankets, towels and so on needed to keep people clean and rested.  A hole in the roof has let in years of rain and snow and dirt.  What is left of once crisp white sheets and warm woolen blankets is now an unspeakable mass of corruption and rot.  There seems something in the very air of this place that causes decay far beyond what one might normally expect."],"exits":[{"to":204,"exit":"go","move":"go white door"}]},
  {"id":224,"x":-320,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House, Cellar Stairs","descriptions":["A narrow landing sits at the top of a rotted wooden staircase.  Above you is a trapdoor and below you is only darkness and musty smells.  You can make out a row of massive objects below but little else."],"exits":[{"to":191,"exit":"go","move":"go small trapdoor"},{"to":225,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden stairs"}]},
  {"id":225,"x":-320,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House Wine Cellar","descriptions":["Dark and shadowed, the room extends a good ways under this part of the building.  Huge casks stand in a row along the brick wall.  One or two evidence some attack as they seem to have been gnawed on.  But by and large, the casks seem intact.  Thick cobwebs stretch between them and all along the walls.  Dust and mold are heavy in the air as is the stink of rotting wine dregs.  A shadowy arch leads deeper into the gloom."],"exits":[{"to":224,"exit":"go","move":"go rickety stairs"},{"to":226,"exit":"go","move":"go shadowy arch"}]},
  {"id":226,"x":-300,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Manor House, Cold Cellar","descriptions":["This room has a surprising chill to it.  Used once for cold storage, it lies abandoned to rot and waste.  You nearly trip over a moldering mess that was once a carcass of meat.  Iron hooks hang from the roof and threaten to impale you if you are not careful.  Once used to hang meat, they are rusty and many are coated with dried blood.  Rotting sacks of root vegetables and grain lie about, apparently left behind and forgotten.  They are ruined by the damp and time."],"exits":[{"to":225,"exit":"go","move":"go shadowy arch"}]},
  {"id":227,"x":-660,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan Trader Outpost","descriptions":["This outpost is a miniature replica of one of the great Trader Guild buildings in the larger towns.  Designed for rapid buying and selling of bulk goods by Guild members, it is crammed and jammed with crates, boxes and packages of all sizes and shapes.  A harried Guild trade minister is at hand to expedite members' transactions and to make sure none of the goods leave under their own power or without the proper fees and monies being exchanged."],"exits":[{"to":118,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Trading Outpost"]},
  {"id":228,"x":-320,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Eastern Riverbed","descriptions":["The Applebrandy flowed in this narrow, deep gorge at one point, plowing a passage that grew deeper through the years until its bed lay in cold shadows never touched by sunshine.  But the river is gone now, and a coat of lush green grass almost as long and thick as bending seaweed covers the ground and walls alike."],"exits":[{"to":230,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":231,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":229,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":229,"x":-340,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Western Riverbed","descriptions":["Erosion along the crumbling bank threatens to erase the empty waterway.  Dotting the sides, gritty silt and jagged furrows give evidence to the slow changing of the land.  Meanwhile, shoots of grass, both fresh and from seasons past, break through the exposed earth in a seemingly futile attempt to fight the effects of time."],"exits":[{"to":228,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":230,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":231,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":230,"x":-320,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Eastern Riverbed","descriptions":["The riverbed stumbles through a series of wavy ruts bearing the accumulation of rich sediment over the passing years.  Colorful calcified deposits cake the walls, narrowing and impeding passage still further.  Far above, a family of knifewrens have made a nest on a small ledge, squawking cheerfully at nothing in particular."],"exits":[{"to":228,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":232,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":233,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":231,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":229,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":231,"x":-340,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Western Riverbed","descriptions":["Knee-high grasses span the width of the broad riverbed, creating the illusion of a smooth continuous flow as the stalks sway on the wind.  A solitary boulder crests the pale green waves like the hump of an old tortoise's shell."],"exits":[{"to":229,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":228,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":230,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":232,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":233,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"aliases":["grass eels","eels"]},
  {"id":232,"x":-320,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Eastern Riverbed","descriptions":["This area of the dried riverbed is choked with debris.  Small sticks, sharp splinters of whitened bone and rusty weapons poke their treacherous teeth above the deep, luxuriant grass.  The floor itself is notably higher in relation to the sloping walls.  An overhanging ledge to the east lies within easy reach."],"exits":[{"to":230,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":233,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":231,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":"go overhanging ledge"}]},
  {"id":233,"x":-340,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Western Riverbed","descriptions":["A stone wall looms over the bank, and rows of neatly tended trees grow beyond the barrier.  Dank leaves, intermixed with an occasional shriveled brown rock, have created layers of composting materials upon the ground.  Clinging to the wind, a faint smell of apples mixes with the aroma of wild grass and detritus filling the gorge."],"exits":[{"to":231,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":230,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":232,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":234,"exit":"go","move":"go rocky incline"}]},
  {"id":234,"x":-340,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Doline","descriptions":["Years of water flowing across the fertile ground eventually caused the soil to succumb to the weight of the world, creating a rather large sinkhole in the riverbed.  The sides of the concave depression slope gently downward towards the middle, where the grassy floor evens out until rising again across the way."],"exits":[{"to":235,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":237,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":236,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":233,"exit":"go","move":"go rocky incline"}]},
  {"id":235,"x":-320,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Doline","descriptions":["Whenever the wind blows, the breeze swirls around inside the sinkhole and stirs the tall grasses like a mixed drink.  Pebbles sporadically rain into the depression from the banks above, only to roll toward the middle and add to the collection of rock fragments already in place.  Unlike the rest of the riverbed, the floor of the doline is somewhat softer due to the disintegrating bedrock beneath the thin layer of green."],"exits":[{"to":237,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":236,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":234,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":236,"x":-340,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Doline","descriptions":["Like a colossal bowl, the ground slants at a gentle gradient toward the center of the area, as if the earth was trying to swallow everything that brazenly adventures into the sinkhole.  Chattering birds occasionally land on the awkward sticks jutting out over the sides of the sinkhole, only to be frightened away by the low, intermittent hissing from the grass below.  The spindly green stalks flinch in spurts and jerks from hidden movement underneath."],"exits":[{"to":234,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":235,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":237,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":237,"x":-320,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Applebrandy River, Doline","descriptions":["Occasional shrieks from flying predators overhead echo all around in the deep sinkhole, filling the space with piercing avian cries of the hunt.  The grass rises up from the rock-strewn ground like the hackles of a dog, tensed as if in response to the movement of creatures underfoot.  Nature never lets silence exist for very long amongst the ever-present flora and fauna."],"exits":[{"to":235,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":236,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":234,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":238,"x":-600,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Exterior","descriptions":["The round base of a massive stone tower rests among the cracked rocks and rubble which have worked their way loose from brittle mortar and have fallen to rest at the great structure's feet.  Silverleaf vines slink up from the dry soil and interweave to form a massive living wall, perhaps the only element bracing the ancient tower from collapsing into a heap of stones and dust.  A gaping archway on the west side of the tower is all that remains of the wooden doorway which once hung there."],"exits":[{"to":100,"exit":"go","move":"go worn path"},{"to":239,"exit":"go","move":"go gaping archway"}],"aliases":["Ancient Tower"]},
  {"id":239,"x":-580,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, First Level","descriptions":["Long brilliant rays of light stream through stone cracks as wide as a barbarian's fist and bounce off the floating dust particles which choke the air and lie thick across the floor.  Even the multitudinous spider webs which span from ceiling to wall to doorway are coated with a thick chalky layer.  A steep spiralling stair is the single standing structure on this first level floor.","The chill night air creeps through stone cracks as wide as a barbarian's fist and fans the floating dust particles which choke the air and lie thick across the floor.  Even the multitudinous spider webs which span from ceiling to wall to doorway are coated with a thick chalky layer.  A steep spiralling stair is the single standing structure on this first level floor."],"exits":[{"to":238,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":240,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiralling stair"}]},
  {"id":240,"x":-560,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Stairwell","descriptions":["Chipped and broken stone steps spiral up and down the round interior of the ancient tower.  Here and there along the walls gaps remain where mighty stone blocks have slipped from their mortar and fallen to the ground below.  You also see some steps leading up and some stairs leading down."],"exits":[{"to":239,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stairs"},{"to":241,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Corveson"]},
  {"id":241,"x":-540,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Stairwell","descriptions":["Chipped and broken stone steps spiral up and down the round interior of the ancient tower.  Here and there along the walls gaps remain where mighty stone blocks have slipped from their mortar and fallen to the ground below."],"exits":[{"to":240,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stairs"},{"to":242,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}]},
  {"id":242,"x":-520,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Stairwell","descriptions":["Chipped and broken stone steps spiral up and down the round interior of the ancient tower.  Here and there along the walls gaps remain where mighty stone blocks have slipped from their mortar and fallen to the ground below."],"exits":[{"to":241,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stairs"},{"to":243,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}]},
  {"id":243,"x":-520,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Stairwell","descriptions":["Chipped and broken stone steps spiral up and down the round interior of the ancient tower.  Here and there along the walls gaps remain where mighty stone blocks have slipped from their mortar and fallen to the ground below."],"exits":[{"to":242,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stairs"},{"to":244,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}]},
  {"id":244,"x":-540,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Stairwell","descriptions":["Chipped and broken stone steps spiral up and down the round interior of the ancient tower.  Here and there along the walls gaps remain where mighty stone blocks have slipped from their mortar and fallen to the ground below."],"exits":[{"to":243,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stairs"},{"to":245,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}]},
  {"id":245,"x":-560,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Abandoned Workshop","descriptions":["Before continuing its up and downward spirals, the staircase breaks open onto a stone platform which may have served at one time as a magical workshop.  Blackened walls, floor, and ceiling speak eloquently of a powerful magic gone awry and backfiring on its caster.  The room is empty but for a single rosewood case, which stands as if left untouched by magic and time."],"exits":[{"to":244,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stairs"},{"to":246,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}],"aliases":["Abandoned Workshop"]},
  {"id":246,"x":-580,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Ancient Tower, Open Air Shrine","descriptions":["The suppressive walls below give way to open air on this top level of the tower.  Great stone columns steadfastly support a battered and weathered roof which has long since lost its shingles to the elements.  The rotted remnants of wooden railings hang limply between columns, having lived out their usefulness years ago."],"exits":[{"to":245,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiraling staircase"}],"aliases":["Telescope"]},
  {"id":247,"x":-460,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Area","descriptions":["The path winds between giant oaks mixed in with a secondary growth of smaller trees of many types.  Your footsteps are hushed on a thick carpet of rotting leaves and pine needles.  The air is fresh with the smell of growing things and rich earth.  The only jarring note is an odd footprint in the dirt.  Of some size, it seems almost human but for its far longer toes ending in deep indentations that speak of non-human claws."],"exits":[{"to":248,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":86,"exit":"go","move":"go gravel road"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":248,"x":-440,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Area","descriptions":["This small clearing is open to the sky but surrounded by a thick growth of trees.  The ground here is soft and shows evidence of recent footsteps.  There is a faint scent of burned wood and ash from the east while several other paths branch off in various directions.  A tall, grotesque totem carved of ironwood dominates the center of the clearing."],"exits":[{"to":249,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":251,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":254,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":247,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":249,"x":-440,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Area","descriptions":["Something has bedded down here lately.  A crude lean-to of branches stripped of their leaves sits in this tiny clearing.  A torn and ruined backpack lies in front of the lean-to and several trees bear scorch marks as if they had been hit by a mage's fire spells.  There is a faint scent of dried blood in the air and hundreds of large flies buzz about in morbid curiosity."],"exits":[{"to":248,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":250,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":250,"x":-460,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Area","descriptions":["The trees grow thick here and the air is heavy and still.  Dried twigs and branches underfoot cause you to move carefully lest a snap give warning to things best left undisturbed.  A partially-gnawed corpse of a small inkhorne deer hangs impaled upon a sharp upthrust branch.  The stench of its corruption thickens the air with a sweetish, vile miasma."],"exits":[{"to":249,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":251,"x":-420,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Firepit","descriptions":["Carved benches of stone and wood circle a firepit in the center of this large clearing.  Your nose tells you that there has been a fire here not too far in the past and a pile of cracked and charred bones suggests whatever lit the fire might not hesitate at taking a try at your own marrow.  You suddenly realize this part of the woods is very quiet, no bird chirps nor does any breeze rustle the leaves.  Crude standards depicting a clenched fist with rust-colored claws surround the clearing."],"exits":[{"to":252,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":248,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":252,"x":-400,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Woodlot","descriptions":["This is an open area, mostly bare of trees.  It appears to have served as the woodlot for the manor as there are stumps everywhere and the ground is littered with scraps and splinters of wood.  A large woodpile left long ago to dry, has become a tangled mess covered with vines and moss.  Huge flat fungi sprout from the stacks of rotting logs."],"exits":[{"to":253,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":251,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":514,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rotting woodpile"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":253,"x":-380,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Barren Spot","descriptions":["Near the protecting outer wall, the earth is barren for some reason.  There is no sign of growth or tree and the soil is a hard and brittle thing with no life in it.  The wall seems in surprisingly good shape.  On this side at least, time has not worked any harm.  Rising too tall to climb, it seems to have done its duty well in protecting this place."],"exits":[{"to":252,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":254,"x":-440,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Path","descriptions":["This path snakes between two close-set trees with low-hanging foliage.  A perfect spot for an ambush, you note to yourself, while trying to stay to the center of the narrow path, away from the shadows and their feeling of watchful menace."],"exits":[{"to":248,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":255,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":255,"x":-440,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Path","descriptions":["The ground here is slightly damp and marshy underfoot.  Several snails laboriously work their way across a large rock, leaving glistening trails of slime.  An odd form of clinging vine has snaked around the trees here and there.  Many heavy loops of it threaten to garrotte you as they dangle along your path among the dense greenery."],"exits":[{"to":254,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":256,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":256,"x":-440,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Wooded Marsh","descriptions":["The ground is low and swampy underfoot.  Each step leaves an imprint in the soil that oozes moisture.  There are heavy vines looped over everything and your footing is unsteady as you try to avoid tripping.  Every bare patch of ground sprouts colonies of dead-white toadstools.  From nearby you hear a deep croaking sound followed by several more in different directions until you stand in the midst of a chorus of frog calls."],"exits":[{"to":255,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":257,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":258,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":257,"x":-420,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Rocky Springs","descriptions":["Standing on relatively firm ground, you note a natural cairn of rocks from which a bubbling spring arises to flow down into the boggy ground south and west.  A tiny pond has formed at the base of the rocks and little water-skimmer insects dart across its smooth surface, dodging each other like frantic ice skaters.  There is a wild and untamed beauty here that earns your respect for whoever first laid out this abandonded park."],"exits":[{"to":259,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":256,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":258,"x":-460,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Marshy Path","descriptions":["Several willow trees grow close together, nearly choking off the pathway.  Somewhere nearby you hear flowing water.  Brightly colored flowers hang from thick-stemmed creepers along the tree trunks, while numerous dragonflies flit among them on jewelled wings.  From time to time a shaft of light fights its way through the greenery and strikes the fliers' wings, causing their intense colors to glisten and sparkle."],"exits":[{"to":256,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":260,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":259,"x":-400,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Rock Outcrop","descriptions":["A large rock outcrop thrusts its way from beneath the boggy soil here, blocking all passage save back towards a nearby spring.  The outcrop rises alongside the outer wall of the preserve but a series of downward- and upward-pointing spikes set near the top discourage any thoughts of rock-climbing today.  Large patches of moss form abstract designs on the granite outcrop and one struggling tree has tried to make a home in a dirt-filled crack in the rock."],"exits":[{"to":257,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":140,"exit":"down","move":"down","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":260,"x":-440,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Stream","descriptions":["The path ends here at a small stream that sings softly to itself as it flows among mossy stones.  Midges and gnats swarm above the water in clouds and they react to your presence with hungry delight.  Looking north along the stream bed you see it flows from beneath a high stone wall.  A tiny fish breaks the water's surface to snag a minute insect for supper."],"exits":[{"to":261,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":258,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":261,"x":-440,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Stream","descriptions":["The stream flows gently from north to south, running along an obviously artificial course.  This place was once meant as a pleasant spot to sit and enjoy the sound, as there is an ancient stone bench, now overturned and broken, set along the stream's edge.  A small hole in the stream bank appears to mark the home of a badger or some other water-dweller."],"exits":[{"to":260,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":262,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":262,"x":-440,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Stream","descriptions":["A stream widens out as it approaches a small river.  The ground is soft and marshy and is heavy with reeds and sedge-grass.  Frogs croak loudly along the banks and one occasionally leaps into the water with a loud splash."],"exits":[{"to":261,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":263,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":263,"x":-460,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Willow Grove and Stream","descriptions":["The stream runs down into a small muddy river, hard by a large grove of willows growing in the rich soil.  As they whisper to each other, long branches brushing the ground in a gentle breeze, it seems to you that there are words and meanings hidden in the idle sounds.  Beneath your feet, the boggy ground shows traces of someone or something else passing by recently."],"exits":[{"to":262,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":264,"x":40,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Northwall Trail, Wooded Grove","descriptions":["The sounds of the river splash through the trees from the southeast, where the woods end abruptly in a tangle of felled trees.  The massive deadfall looks like the remains of some giant creature, its weather-bleached bones laying in a great heap beside the river.","The sounds of the river splash through the trees to the southeast, where the tangled trunks of a massive deadfall laying along the riverbank glow a ghostly pale in the moonlight."],"exits":[{"to":221,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["N Gate"],"linksTo":"Map6_Crossing_North_Gate.xml"},
  {"id":265,"x":20,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Crossing, North Wall Battlements","descriptions":["Rounding the city's northwestern-most point, the cobbled walkway stretches a short distance before being interrupted by an unfinished section of the town wall.  Although a stack of felled trees evidences the logging in progress, the forest is still perilously close to the new defenses and provides would-be attackers protective cover."],"exits":[{"to":266,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":220,"exit":"climb","move":"climb break"},{"to":221,"exit":"climb","move":"climb jagged embrasure"}],"linksTo":"Map1_Crossing.xml"},
  {"id":266,"x":0,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Crossing, West Gate Battlements","descriptions":["The fitted stone of the town walls intersects in a curved angle, one side becoming the western wall and the other stretching out against the northern border of the town.  From this vantage point above the West Gate, a warrior can watch for enemies breaking from the cover of the northern forest or sweeping up from the grassy plains to the southwest."],"exits":[{"to":265,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":267,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":1,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow embrasure"},{"to":266,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone stairs"}],"linksTo":"Map1_Crossing.xml"},
  {"id":267,"x":0,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Crossing, West Wall Battlements","descriptions":["The cobbled pavement atop the walkway crumbles into the unfinished wall as it stretches south toward the Segoltha River.  The view over the wall of lush grassland and farms is a stark contrast to the sight of the slums and squalid buildings that line Kertigen Road."],"exits":[{"to":266,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":2,"exit":"climb","move":"climb low embrasure"},{"to":267,"exit":"go","move":"go enclosed lean-to"}],"linksTo":"Map1_Crossing.xml"},
  {"id":268,"x":-40,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Neighborhood Entrance","descriptions":["A pair of stone pillars mark the edge of the neighborhood named Temple Hill.  A freshly graded, crushed-stone street carries traffic south into the heart of the community.  Running along one side of the lane, a low stone wall, cut with a prominent wrought iron gate, borders the grounds of Temple Hill Manor.  Across the street are a row of neat stone cottages."],"exits":[{"to":269,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":2,"exit":"go","move":"go stone pillars"},{"to":287,"exit":"go","move":"go wrought gate"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Temple Hill"]},
  {"id":269,"x":-40,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["The crushed stone of the lane leads between several stone cottages, winding its way deeper into the district.  Young locust trees have been planted along both sides of the road in the hopes that with the passage of time they will shade the way."],"exits":[{"to":268,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":270,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":288,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":270,"x":-20,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill Lane, Salvage Stoneworks","descriptions":["With lights dimmed for the night, somber cottages stand across from a large industrial workshop that dominates the south side of the lane.  Just visible in the weak light behind the large building is a chute leading down from a quarry that lifts strange vertical shadows into the night sky.","Lazy clouds of dust occasionally billow out from a large stoneworking shop dominating the south side of Temple Hill Lane.  Behind the workshop, loose rock and unprocessed rubble tumbles down a large chute from a partially visible quarrying area."],"exits":[{"to":271,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":269,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":285,"exit":"climb","move":"climb chute"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":271,"x":0,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["Dark iron lanterns hung from tall poles glow softly against the darkness of night.  A scattering of pots and vases leave shadows against the somber walls of the homes.","Carefully tended lawns and young trees provide evidence that the residents of this neighborhood are planting and planning for the future.  Stone and brick cottages line the lane, with somber colors predominating -- mostly dark greys, dark browns, and dull reds, although the trimmings and trappings suggest the inhabitants are not nearly as gloomy as their dwellings."],"exits":[{"to":272,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":273,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":270,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":272,"x":40,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["Lawns and gardens stretch out alongside stone cottages that stand in rows along the lane.  Small trees and plantings decorate the well-tended lawns, but none are of any immense size.  Evidently, the temple rubble provides better building material than soil for planting."],"exits":[{"to":275,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":271,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":273,"x":0,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Memorial Park","descriptions":["Grass surrounds a small reflecting pool in this wooded park at the top of the hill.  Strategically placed low stone benches surround the pool, allowing peaceful contemplation of life.  Roses twine along a fence that separates the park from the quarry to the east."],"exits":[{"to":271,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":274,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":284,"exit":"go","move":"go grassy path"},{"to":286,"exit":"climb","move":"climb low fence"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":274,"x":40,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Memorial Park","descriptions":["Jagged stone makes a staggered path through this restful park.  Tall trees reach out to the sky and give homes to squirrels, rabbits and a variety of birds.  A lone stone bench, flanked on each side by a pot of fragrant flowers, offers a place for quiet reflection."],"exits":[{"to":273,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":282,"exit":"go","move":"go staggered path"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":275,"x":60,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["Brightly lit stone cottages throw light almost everywhere on the darkened street except for one rubble-strewn lot, leaving it in the shadows.  An unusually sturdy fence, immediately noticeable even in the dim light, surrounds the area.","Cozy, sturdy white cottages line the crushed-stone street, with the exception of one cordoned-off lot.  The fence surrounding it is quite sturdy, and has been patched and reinforced to prevent even the most agile of children from wandering into the area."],"exits":[{"to":276,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":272,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":276,"x":80,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["Stolid cottages stand in the darkness of the crushed stone street bending around the hill.  A cluster of lighted windows are visible downhill, backed by the shadowy mass of the city wall and the lights of the Crossing twinkling in the inky darkness beyond.","The street turns to follow the contour of Temple Hill, providing a good view from the high vantage point.  Downhill lies a small court with a statue in the center.  Rising behind it are the earthen ramparts of the Crossing, the roofs of the city peeking over the top of the wall."],"exits":[{"to":277,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":278,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":275,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":277,"x":100,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Battle Bell Court","descriptions":["Snuggled between trees, hills, and the city wall, the tranquil court rests quietly in the night.  Graceful cottages cluster around a huge iron bell hung from a decorative stone tower.  Candles carefully placed within the tower lend a soft warm glow to the bell within.","The clamor of commerce from around the West Gate carries from beyond the city wall, but this tranquil court is well screened from view among the trees.  Graceful cottages cluster around a huge iron bell hung from a decorative stone tower."],"exits":[{"to":276,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":278,"x":80,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["Carefully arranged cottages surround a stone pedestal topped by a glass case.  The many lights of the Crossing glisten to the east, while a thoughtfully placed lantern highlights a bronze plaque and the contents of the glass case.","Cottages surround a simply carved stone pedestal in the center of the lane.  A glass case surmounts the pedestal, with a bronze plaque mounted firmly on the front.  Downhill to the east, a great expanse of rooftops stretches out behind the earthen mass of the Crossing city wall."],"exits":[{"to":276,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":279,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":279,"x":80,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Temple Hill Lane","descriptions":["Scents of cedar and pine drift upon the air, perhaps from the fires of the nearby homes.  Soft rustlings of night creatures mingle with faint owl hoots and form a serene melody.  To the east, the twinkling lights of Crossing contrast with the closer black bulk of the city wall.","Scents of fresh bread and baked goods drift upon the air, perhaps from one of the nearby homes.  Sounds of children playing mingle with bird song and form a pleasant melody.  The cozy cottages here have a sweeping view of the Crossing wall below with the city beyond."],"exits":[{"to":278,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":281,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":280,"exit":"go","move":"go crushed path"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":280,"x":80,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Captain's Court","descriptions":["A small pond in the middle of this quiet, restful court sports tiny boats upon its surface.  Outdoor lanterns from the surrounding cottages give a nice, soft glow to the surrounding shrubs and flowers.  Taller trees loom to the south as an occasional sleepy birdcall sounds in the darkness.","Laughter rings loud as children play with boats upon a small pond.  Each cottage in this pleasant court faces the pond and has a different flag hung from its eaves.  To the south grows a more densely wooded area that offers the children more exciting play."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"go","move":"go crushed path"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":281,"x":60,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["The low, yellowish vegetation of the lane gives way to deeper greens and larger shrubs, partially masking the gentle slope to the south.  One young lunat tree seems to be thriving, although it still stands only about as tall as a Gor'Tog."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":282,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":282,"x":40,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["The stately manors constructed high on Temple Hill enjoy a broad view of the Mycthengelde Flatlands and the roofs of the Crossing.  The dense city lights of the Crossing create a dull glow overhead that contrasts notably with the scattered cottage lights along Finch Cottage Path down beyond a narrow stone path.","The stately manors constructed high on Temple Hill enjoy a broad view of the Mycthengelde Flatlands and the roofs of the Crossing.  Rows of colorful flowers and shrubs encircle each manor and give them a distinctive look.  A narrow stone path leads south towards Finch Cottage Path."],"exits":[{"to":281,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":283,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":274,"exit":"go","move":"go grassy path"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":283,"x":20,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["Cheery glows emanate from the windows of stone cabins lining Hero's March, echoed by a small glimmer of lights from the Crossing to the east.  A scattering of cabin lights twinkle to the south through the thick undergrowth.","Cottages lining the crushed rubble surface of Hero's March have expansive views of Finch Cottage Path and a tiny glimpse of the Crossing's western wall.  Clusters of homes, visible as roofs and chimneys, poke through the lush vegetation below while birdsong drifts on the air."],"exits":[{"to":282,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":284,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":284,"x":0,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["A heavy cast iron sundial is centered in the middle of the crushed stone path, a low dark shape in the dimness.  Occasional gleams of light like bright gold shine from cottage windows or doors.  Nearly invisible in the shadows between two cottages, a grassy path winds uphill.","A heavy cast iron sundial is centered in middle of the crushed stone path, surrounded by a narrow ring of low-growing herbs.  Occasionally a bird swoops down to land on it, as if checking the time.  Between two cottages, a grassy path winds uphill."],"exits":[{"to":283,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":292,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":291,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":273,"exit":"go","move":"go grassy path"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":285,"x":-20,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Salvage Quarry","descriptions":["Piles of stone and pieces of machinery stand silently in the darkness.  Along the west edge of the quarry the dust of the day's work has settled upon the machines in a thick layer opposite piles of sorted material.  A cliff stands to the south, forming a tall backdrop to the scene.","Workers sort the salvaged stone of the quarry into piles of similar size and color.  Along the west edge of the pit, stone is pounded and poured through stacked sieves to make various grades of sand and gravel.  Finished materials are stacked along the side of the quarry until needed, when they are slid down a large chute to the stone works.  Every few minutes, warning shouts precede a great tumbling of raw materials from a cliff to the south."],"exits":[{"to":286,"exit":"climb","move":"climb short cliff"},{"to":270,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone chute"}]},
  {"id":286,"x":-20,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Salvage Quarry","descriptions":["Tall stone faces loom above three sides of the quarry, standing stark in the night.  Occasionally small stones slide down from the treacherous rock walls, echoing loudly as they reach the bottom and bounce over a low cliff.","Tall faces of variegated stone loom above the observer on three sides of the quarry.  Workers pry mixed stone and rubble from these rock walls, sending it tumbling into piles which are then shoved over a small cliff to the north for sorting."],"exits":[{"to":285,"exit":"climb","move":"climb small cliff"},{"to":273,"exit":"climb","move":"climb quarry face"}]},
  {"id":287,"x":-60,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill Manor, Grounds","descriptions":["Framed by a low stone wall pierced with a wrought iron gate, a grand lawn stretches out along three sides of Temple Hill Manor to gracefully encompass the elegant abode.  Low plantings form dark hummocks on the lawn, and young trees throw thin dark shadows across the front of the manor.  Two bronze statues set on stone pedestals hold places of honor on the great lawn.","Framed by a low stone wall pierced with a wrought iron gate, a grand lawn stretches out along three sides of Temple Hill Manor to gracefully encompass the elegant abode.  Small plantings dot the grass, drawing attention toward the young maple trees flanking the door of the manor.  Two bronze statues set on stone pedestals hold places of honor on the great lawn, further enhancing the elegant setting."],"exits":[{"to":268,"exit":"go","move":"go wrought gate"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":288,"x":-40,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["The taller vegetation of the Mycthengelde Flatlands grows close against the hill below this stretch of Hero's March.  Darkness and shadows create an illusion that the Mycthengelde treetops are but an extension of Temple Hill.  Stone cottages cluster along the dark gravel of the street, their windows throwing a welcome light on the comforting scene.","The Mycthengelde Flatlands encroach upon the base of Temple Hill just below this stretch of Hero's March, with the tallest trees almost an extension of the hill.  Stone cottages cluster along the gravel surface of the way, the solid houses and well-maintained street lending a sense of permanence to the area.  Children shout as they sport among the cottages, their noises echoed by the noise of stone falling in a nearby quarry."],"exits":[{"to":269,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":289,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":289,"x":-70,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["Low plantings form lines and odd geometric figures on the lawns that surround the gaily lit stone cottages.  A few raised beds sport taller varieties of vegetation that draw thick shadows around them in the embrace of the night.","Yellowish-green lawns and shrubs stretch in front of cozy stone cottages, green only where the owners have imported soil or planted raised beds.  In spite of the yellow color, the residents of this area are enthusiastic gardeners as shown by the attention to their landscaping."],"exits":[{"to":288,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":290,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":290,"x":-55,"y":145,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["A broad view of the Mycthengelde Flatlands looms emptily to the west, fading into the dark night.  Pristine cottages face a tall marble fountain whose surface is lit by carefully placed lamps.  Thick shrubs and pale flowers rustle in the breeze and send fragrant scents into the air.","Pristine cottages line each side of the path and enjoy a pleasant view of a tall marble fountain and the surrounding flatlands.  A memorial plaque upon the fountain hails warriors from seasons past.  Thick shrubs and pale flowers grace each home with sweet smells and a touch of elegance."],"exits":[{"to":291,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":289,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":291,"x":-40,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Hero's March","descriptions":["Colorful cottages line the crushed rock street and enjoy a panoramic view of the Mycthengelde Flatlands.  Young trees, freshly planted, lift up their scrawny limbs to the sky.  One such tree enjoys a ragtag doll hanging haphazardly from its highest point.","Pristine cottages line each side of the path and enjoy a pleasant view of a tall marble fountain and the surrounding flatlands.  A memorial plaque upon the fountain hails warriors from seasons past.  Thick shrubs and pale flowers grace each home with sweet smells and a touch of elegance."],"exits":[{"to":284,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":290,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":292,"x":0,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Finch Cottage Path","descriptions":["Finch Cottage Path represents a drastic change from Temple Hill proper.  The soil is old and deep here, and vegetation flourishes.  Care was taken when building the cottages to leave as many of the original plants as possible.  The occasional ruffle of feathers reveals the presence of a flock of birds roosting for the night in the thick shrubbery of the area.","Finch Cottage Path represents a drastic change from Temple Hill proper.  The soil is old and deep here, and vegetation flourishes.  Care was taken when building the cottages to leave as many of the original plants as possible.  Numerous songbirds flit and chirp among the abundant shrubs and trees, a living reward for the careful preservation of plants."],"exits":[{"to":284,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":293,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":293,"x":20,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Finch Cottage Path","descriptions":["Soft breezes carry over a wide tan circle of crushed stone and slip into the surrounding wyndwood trees, producing a soothing music of rustling leaves as they pass.  Snug cottages tuck themselves beneath the tangled tree limbs that lean in over the circle.  A platform birdfeeder on a tall pole in the middle of the circle stands lonesome in the night, waiting for birds to arrive with the dawn.","A number of paths converge upon a wide tan circle of crushed stone surrounded by twisting wyndwood trees.  Snug cottages tuck themselves beneath the tangled tree limbs that reach out over the circle.  Birds dart about from tree to bush to shrub, pausing frequently at the cedar platform birdfeeder on a tall pole that stands at the center of the circle."],"exits":[{"to":294,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":295,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":292,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":294,"x":40,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Pine Finch Circle","descriptions":["The path ends in a dim grove of trees with scattered lights originating from a small circle of cottages centered about a tall cedar platform birdfeeder.  The cottages are nestled beneath the canopies of tall old trees and almost disappear into shadows of the trees behind luxuriant stands of low plants.  Soft, irregular sounds disclose the presence of birds hidden for the night in the thick undergrowth.","The path ends in a grove of trees containing a small circle of cottages centered about a tall cedar platform birdfeeder.  The cottages are nestled beneath the canopies of tall old trees and surrounded by luxuriant stands of low plants.  Birds sprint from place to place in a flurry of wings, pausing from time to time at the birdfeeder."],"exits":[{"to":293,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":295,"x":0,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Finch Cottage Path","descriptions":["Lunat trees loom tall and shadowy over the path meandering between the warmly lit cottages snugly situated in thick stands of shrubs.  The tree-lined path continues to the south, while a smaller path branches off to the northwest.  The dense shrubbery emits an occasional drowsy chirp that hints at the notable avian population of the area.","Lunat trees line the elegant path meandering between the comfortable-looking cottages snugly situated in thick stands of shrubs.  The tree-lined path continues to the south, while a smaller path branches off to the northwest.  Birds dart between shrubs and trees, while birdsong rings out in a near-constant flow of music."],"exits":[{"to":293,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":297,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":296,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":296,"x":-20,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Goldfinch Circle","descriptions":["The path dead-ends into a cozy circle of homes throwing warm light through their windows into a small clearing.  Cottages nearly disappear in thick growths of native plants and the landscaping gathers odd shadows in the dim light.  A cedar platform birdfeeder stands on a tall pole in the middle of the clearing, bereft of winged visitors by night.","The path dead-ends into a cozy circle of homes clustered around a small clearing edged with wildflowers.  Comfortable cottages are nestled among native plants and lush landscaping tended with loving care.  Birds flit about the luxurious vegetation, pausing at a cedar platform birdfeeder on a tall pole."],"exits":[{"to":295,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":297,"x":0,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Finch Cottage Path","descriptions":["The graceful path winds among cheerily lit stone cottages nestled in thickets of vegetation.  One notable oak stands paternally near the path, a tall feeder hanging from its branches just visible in the dim light thrown out by the homes.","The graceful path winds between stone cottages nestled in comforting thickets of vegetation.  Chirping echoes around the cottages as birds dart in and out amongst the shrubs.  A long sunflower feeder hangs from a sprawling old oak, providing a royal feast for visiting birds."],"exits":[{"to":295,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":298,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":299,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":298,"x":20,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, House Finch Circle","descriptions":["Tall shrubs and heavy vegetation grow in lush profusion around cozy stone cottages set in a rough circle.  Light from the cabin windows coalesces upon a large birdfeeder on a tall pole -- evidently the local entertainment.","Native plants and bird-friendly vegetation grow in lush profusion around cozy stone cottages.  A large oak birdfeeder on a tall pole creates a focus for the cabins -- evidently bird watching is a common local interest."],"exits":[{"to":297,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":299,"x":-20,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Finch Cottage Path","descriptions":["Lunat trees cast long shadows over the path that narrows as it continues toward the southwest, slipping between cozy cottages pleasantly located in stands of tended vegetation.  A faint sound from the surrounding undergrowth provides evidence of the noteworthy number of birds found in the neighborhood.","Lunat trees line the elegant path that narrows as it continues toward the southwest, slipping between cozy cottages pleasantly located in stands of tended vegetation.  Birds gambol in the air between trees on either side of the path and birdcalls ring out with a merry chatter from the surrounding undergrowth."],"exits":[{"to":297,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":300,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":300,"x":-40,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Temple Hill, Finch Cottage Grounds","descriptions":["Tall shrubbery dominates the landscaping around Finch Cottage, appearing denser in the dark.  Occasionally, rustling sounds and the rare sleepy birdcalls can be heard coming from the bushes.  A long feeder hangs in front of one window, waiting for birds to arrive with the dawn.","The Finch Cottage grounds are carefully landscaped to attract birds.  Shrubs and berry bushes provide food and sanctuary, and nest boxes hung about the yard provide cozy homes.  Finches abound, attracted to a long hanging feeder in front of the cottage's window."],"exits":[{"to":299,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":301,"x":-700,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Small, bent satinwoods cling to the rocky slope, their gnarled roots seeking patches of soil.  Tiny purple flowers spread across the ground, thriving and flourishing where the larger and greedier trees barely hang on.  A path levels out to the northwest, following the curve of the outcrop, while to the southwest the way continues on up."],"exits":[{"to":303,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":302,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rutted cliff"}]},
  {"id":302,"x":-700,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A huge rocky outcrop breaks through the thick, loamy soil of the forest as the ground rises and roughens.  Fewer trees grow up here, and those that do cling to what soil they can find are smaller and twisted.  Graceful ferns and lacy grey moss spread across the exposed rocks, softening their harsh outlines."],"exits":[{"to":301,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rutted cliff"},{"to":103,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steep trail"}],"aliases":["Rocky Outcrop"]},
  {"id":303,"x":-720,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A narrow stony shelf runs along one edge of the rocky outcrop, winding among boulders and gaps and the occasional stunted tree.  The view down to the east is green, a dense tree canopy only a short distance below.  Small grey birds dart back and forth between the trees, quarreling over something."],"exits":[{"to":301,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":304,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":304,"x":-740,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A gnarled satinwood tree grows jammed into a shadowy corner, its stunted branches reaching up to the sky.  Ferns rustle in the cold night breeze, punctuated by the call of a distant bird hunting somewhere in the blackness.","A gnarled satinwood grows jammed into a rocky corner, its stunted branches reaching up out of the shadow, seeking the sun.  Yellowish ferns carpet the ground wherever a patch of soil lies, in crevices around the bare grey rocks."],"exits":[{"to":305,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":303,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":305,"x":-740,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A tangle of trees and shrubs growing in a deep patch of soil forces the path dangerously near the ledge to the east.  The rocky outcrop drops away, giving a view of a vast, dense forest.  Opposite the ledge, the rock rises up high overhead, the grey stone climbable only by spreading lichen and moss."],"exits":[{"to":306,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":304,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":306,"x":-740,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Millenia of streaming rain have cut vertical grooves into the solid rock of the outcrop.  Looking like the scored bark of some huge grey tree, the grooved stone runs down the rock face into a shadowy hollow."],"exits":[{"to":305,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":307,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":326,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":307,"x":-760,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A cool breeze blows past the rocky outcrop and up the slope to the west.  Between the breeze and the perpetual shade here on the north side, it's rather chilly.  The trees don't seem to mind, though, nor do the scrubby bushes that cling to the rocky soil."],"exits":[{"to":306,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":308,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":308,"x":-780,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The footing is treacherous here on this particularly steep stretch of winding path.  The trail turns south as it climbs higher, while the lower reaches are down to the east.  Not even bushes grow in this immediate area -- all is steep cliff and featureless rock, with a narrow trail made even more harrowing by gusting winds."],"exits":[{"to":318,"exit":"go","move":"go twisty trail"},{"to":307,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":309,"x":-720,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A few stunted satinwood trees grow in the shallow soil up here on the outcrop.  Yellow-green grass and a few thornbushes fill in the space between the trees.  The bushes occasionally emit a rustling which isn't the product of the stiff breeze -- apparently some sort of small animal makes its home in this area, in whatever cover it can find."],"exits":[{"to":327,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":310,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":310,"x":-740,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A deeper patch of soil is home to a stand of lush bushes with ruffled blue flowers the size of an orange.  Small paw prints lead in and out of the bushes, with an occasional larger paw print showing that predators live here too.  Scruffy looking weeds grow in the rocky soil a distance from the bushes, and very little at all grows up the trail to the west, higher on the outcrop."],"exits":[{"to":309,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":311,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":332,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":311,"x":-760,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["This arm of the trail is wide and relatively flat, running between the northern and southern domes of the rocky outcrop.  Tough grass grows all about, and some bushes and an occasional satinwood tree grow here and there about the landscape.  The soil isn't very deep, nor very fertile, and the satinwoods aren't the healthiest specimens, but they persevere, as life always does, and they manage to survive the harsh conditions."],"exits":[{"to":310,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":312,"exit":"go","move":"go twisting trail"}]},
  {"id":312,"x":-780,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The northern lobe of the outcrop rises high above, even though this intersection itself is nowhere near ground level.  A spindly looking satinwood tree grows on the slope below and to the east, blocking most of the view in that direction.  No birds flutter in its branches -- the only creatures immediately visible on the tree are some black ants, marching in a line along one of its nearer limbs.  Some large claw marks in the bark suggest that larger animals are about, however."],"exits":[{"to":320,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":311,"exit":"go","move":"go twisting trail"},{"to":313,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":313,"x":-800,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The two mounds of the rocky outcropping cast deep shadows on this narrow gap hardly any light penetrates, even from the stars.  A few ferns and a scrubby bush rustle in the breeze.","Little light penetrates this narrow gap between the two mounds of the outcropping.  Grey rock soars toward the sky to the north and south, with a deep, treacherous looking crevasse in between to the immediate south of the trail.  A few sickly ferns grow in gaps and chinks in the rock, and a scrubby bush with poisonous looking berries clings to one side of the slope."],"exits":[{"to":312,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":314,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow trace"}]},
  {"id":314,"x":-820,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Piles of rubble indicate frequent rockslides on this side of the outcrop.  The loose boulders and rocks and pebbles make footing treacherous.  A narrow trail leads the eye up and to the northeast, toward the ridge crest.  Silhouetted trees whip back and forth in what appear to be strong winds."],"exits":[{"to":315,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":321,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow trail"},{"to":313,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow trace"}]},
  {"id":315,"x":-840,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Coarse vines like grey-green twine cling to what little soil is to be found in hollows and chinks of the rock.  Fireflies swirl and swoop in glowing spirals over the night-darkened vegetation, striving to attract mates with their luminous dance while at the same time avoiding night-hunting predators.","Tiny star-shaped flowers in purple and yellow dot coarse vines that cling, like grey-green twine, to what little soil is to be found in hollows and chinks of the rock.  A few hearty insects, always thriving wherever there's even a ghost of life, march among the flowers.  Some collect pollen or nectar, while others prey upon their neighbors."],"exits":[{"to":316,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":314,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":324,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":316,"x":-840,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The trail winds around this northern lobe of the rocky outcrop, and a smaller path makes its way up to the eastern ridge.  Low bushes with grey-green leaves grow here and there on the slope, finding whatever pockets of soil there may be.  Occasional rustling sounds from the bushes suggest some sort of animal life, although if there are any small creatures here, they stay well hidden."],"exits":[{"to":317,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":315,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":323,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rocky ridge"}]},
  {"id":317,"x":-820,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A pile of white bones and a few shreds of rotting hide suggest that something had a good meal not too long ago.  A scrap of what looks like a hare's ear lies to one side, and the bones are about the right size to have been a hare.  Large paw prints cover the ground around the carcass, but they're too overlapped to show where the predator went."],"exits":[{"to":318,"exit":"go","move":"go twisting trace"},{"to":316,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":318,"x":-800,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The view to the northwest is grand at this elevation, with the landscape spread out like a patchwork quilt.  An eagle soars in the distance, keeping a sharp eye out for prey on the distant ground.  Closer in, the path curves east and west around the boundary of the rocky outcrop.  Sea level is far below, and most of the surfaces within immediate reach are vertical."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":317,"exit":"go","move":"go twisting trace"},{"to":308,"exit":"go","move":"go twisty trail"}]},
  {"id":319,"x":-780,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Stringy creepers spread out across the rock like a fisherman's net spread to dry.  Ragged bell-shaped blossoms in a pale yellow decorate the vines, their petals glowing in the starlight.  Fireflies swirl and dance above the flowers, leaving glowing afterimages in the blackness.  Down in the dry dirt among the creepers is a large paw print, suggesting that creatures larger than fireflies do frequent this place.","Stringy creepers spread out across the rock like a fisherman's net spread to dry.  Ragged bell-shaped blossoms in a pale yellow decorate the vines, their faces turned up to the sun like little cups.  A dull yellow butterfly flutters from one flower to the next, collecting what little nectar they manage to produce.  Down in the dry dirt among the creepers is a large paw print, suggesting that creatures larger than butterflies do frequent this place."],"exits":[{"to":320,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":318,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":325,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":320,"x":-780,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The path runs straight north and south here, scoured clean of dirt by the gusting wind.  A narrower trail, out of the wind but rough with loose stones, winds its way down the slope to the east.  Farther east and much closer to the ground, a deep green forest spreads across the land.  Farther yet, beyond the forest, are the regular, colored patches that mark croplands.  A tiny village is barely discernable as an irregular blotch in the rectangular blocks of fieldland."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":312,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":321,"x":-800,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Ridge","descriptions":["An intrepid bird has made a nest high up in one of the stunted trees.  The nest is a marvel of engineering, clinging to the branches with grass and vines and mud-plaster.  That it's survived the steady, strong winds way up here speaks well of the stubborn bird who built it."],"exits":[{"to":322,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":314,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow trail"}]},
  {"id":322,"x":-800,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Ridge","descriptions":["Wind-blown grit has sculpted the stone into fanciful shapes, scouring out the softer stone and leaving the harder layers ridged and twisted.  One spire looks rather like a chess piece, from the right angle.","Wind-blown grit has sculpted the stone into fanciful shapes, scouring out the softer stone and leaving the harder layers ridged and twisted.  One spire looks rather like a chess piece from the right angle."],"exits":[{"to":321,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":323,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":323,"x":-820,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Ridge","descriptions":["The winds whip through the branches of the short, stunted trees up here on the ridge line.  It's uncomfortably cold, and eyes watering from the wind can't even properly appreciate the view.  Footing is good, since the wind has blown away loose stones and soil, leaving only what is well-anchored."],"exits":[{"to":322,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":316,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rocky ridge"}]},
  {"id":324,"x":-840,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Slope","descriptions":["The slope on this side of the outcrop is just barely navigable, about down to here.  The drop-off farther to the west is vertical, and the thought of climbing down it is unpleasant.  The view is spectacular, however, and the western lands spread out from one horizon to the other are awe-inspiring in their beauty and variety."],"exits":[{"to":315,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":325,"x":-760,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Notch","descriptions":["This narrow notch between two huge rocks is home to nothing more complex than some yellowish grass and a bit of lacy grey moss that blends nearly invisibly into the stone.  Little light penetrates here, and the atmosphere is bare and gloomy.  The only positive note about this place is that the same rocks which shade it also block the winds."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":326,"x":-720,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Shaded Hollow","descriptions":["Lush green ferns line this hollow in the rock.  The soil is thicker here, with the dry bed of a tiny stream, probably carved by flowing rain water, running down from above and disappearing into a dry, cracked basin.  Towering stone rises high overhead in every direction, making this hollow uncomfortably cool even though it's protected from the wind."],"exits":[{"to":306,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":327,"x":-720,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The view to the east, of lush, green forest and a glistening brook, is a sharp contrast to the harsher landscape in the immediate area.  The deep, fertile soil of the forest is only a wish up here, where the ground is rocky and dry, with little loam in it.  Plants are smaller, tougher, and less colorful than down on the flatlands."],"exits":[{"to":309,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":328,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":328,"x":-740,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The trail west leads up, higher onto the outcrop.  The breeze down here is cool and strong, but the branches of trees further up whip back and forth as though possessed by demons.  Just looking up at it makes one feel cold.  A smaller trail leading down to the southwest looks treacherous, but at least it doesn't look quite so chilly down there."],"exits":[{"to":327,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":330,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":329,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":329,"x":-740,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Crumbly Ledge","descriptions":["This ledge feels like it's about to fall off the rock face at any time.  Tough grass grows in the soil captured by cracks in the rock, and the roots of the plants pry, very slowly, at the stone, forcing it farther and farther apart.  Some day it'll give, and the ledge, and anything -- or any one -- on it will plunge down onto the flatlands below."],"exits":[{"to":328,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":330,"x":-740,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The wind up here finds every gap and chink in clothing, armor, and anything else one might wrap up in.  The plant life, at least, doesn't seem to mind and other plants grow low to the ground.  No extravagant explosions of leaf or flower here -- everything is small, sturdy, and functional."],"exits":[{"to":331,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":328,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":331,"x":-740,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A wide spot in the trail invites a rest, and a clear view to the east invites a long, admiring look.  A verdant forest spreads out immediately below the rocky outcrop, stitched with the narrow thread of a glittering brook across its middle.  Beyond the forest lies cropland, planted in greens and browns and beiges, laid out like a game board.  A small village lies far to the east, nestled among the fields and orchards."],"exits":[{"to":330,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":332,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":332,"x":-760,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A patch of white puffy flowers spreads out across the ground, their dark green tendrils seeking out soil and water.  One mound of flowers looks like it's been chewed on, and some small paw prints in the dirt confirm the impression."],"exits":[{"to":331,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":333,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":310,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":333,"x":-780,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A crooked intersection in the trail splits the way into three branches.  A flat path runs east, and seems to be the easiest way to go.  A narrower trail winds up the side of the outcrop to the south, while a gap between a couple of rocks to the southwest leads down into shadow.  The ground here is scoured clean of soil by the winds, and there are no tracks to indicate which path might be the more heavily travelled."],"exits":[{"to":332,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":334,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite rockface"},{"to":480,"exit":"climb","move":"climb twisted vine"}]},
  {"id":334,"x":-800,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The steep trail takes a turn here, curving from the north to the southwest as it climbs.  Loose rock and pebbles make the footing uncertain, requiring complete concentration.  An occasional howling cry, blasting through the cold air, makes concentration difficult, however."],"exits":[{"to":335,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":333,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite rockface"}]},
  {"id":335,"x":-820,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The trail winds around a slab of grey rock that thrusts into the air like a watchtower.  The winds are sharp this high up, slicing like frozen knives into every chink and opening in clothing or armor.  The only plants are low-growing, strongly rooted, or both. "],"exits":[{"to":336,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":340,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":334,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"aliases":["young ogres"]},
  {"id":336,"x":-800,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Looking down from the crest of the rocky outcrop, the change of terrain between the rocks and the forest is obvious.  The dominant color on this side is grey -- grey rocks and grey-green foliage, spotted with occasional patches of dusty color where ever a plant has decided to put up flowers.  On the forest side the dominant color is a rich green, where lush trees and grass and ferns blend with larger and more colorful flowers."],"exits":[{"to":337,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":335,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":337,"x":-780,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A patch of low thornbushes crowns the rock at the base of a taller spire.  Sheltered somewhat from the wind, the bushes have managed to spread out and grow to about waist high.  Despite the lack of wind on this side of the spire, however, the bushes sway and rustle -- apparently something else has also taken advantage of the calmer air and the shelter of the foliage."],"exits":[{"to":338,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":336,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":338,"x":-780,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["The biting winds draw tears to the eyes, but the view to the east is worth some discomfort.  Directly below stands a lush forest, spread out like a deep green ribbon with a silver thread of water running through it.  Patches of fields and orchards stretch from the edge of the wood to the eastern horizon, marred only by a tiny blotch of town.  Far to the east, the smoke from dozens, or perhaps even hundreds of fires rises into the air, forming a foggy haze.","Strong winds howl through the blackness of the night, finding unimagined gaps in clothing and armor.  Spread to the east is only more blackness, but lit by a few lights, here and there.  One is relatively close, east and a bit south, a small flicker indicating a band or perhaps a small village.  Slightly larger is the flickering glow from farther east, about halfway from here to the horizon.  And on the horizon itself is a spot that lights up a patch of land as broad as an outstretched hand. "],"exits":[{"to":337,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":339,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":339,"x":-800,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["Tiny purple flowers cover the rocky summit.  Their mossy green foliage grows low to the ground, their roots digging in deep in search of both water and anchorage.  A few patches of the mossy plants look crushed or nibbled, but no loose soil is allowed to collect here, and there are no tracks to indicate what might have been browsing."],"exits":[{"to":338,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":340,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":340,"x":-820,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop","descriptions":["A single gnarled satinwood stands here, bent and twisted by the wind until it resembles nothing so much as a gnarled hand growing out of the rocky soil, all its fingers yearning toward the west.  A few low, mossy plants cling to its roots, sending up tiny purple flowers a bare fingerwidth above the ground."],"exits":[{"to":335,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":339,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":341,"x":-160,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Meek","descriptions":["Large rocks lie here and there, partially buried in the moist soil.  Dense foliage grows low to the ground, covered with tiny droplets of condensation.  A deep red vine clings to tree trunks, its tiny yellow blossoms giving off a pungent aroma."],"exits":[{"to":343,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":342,"exit":"go","move":"go faint path"}]},
  {"id":342,"x":-160,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Mycthengelde, Flatlands","descriptions":["The ground is inclined here at the foot of the Siergelde.  The trail becomes indistinguishable as it disappears between low-growing shrubs and a thick grove of trees.  To the north, the trees give way to grassy plains."],"exits":[{"to":13,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":341,"exit":"go","move":"go path"}]},
  {"id":343,"x":-180,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Meek","descriptions":["You pick your way cautiously over the rocky floor of the forest grove.  A warm dampness swirls about you, causing your clothes to stick to your skin.  You notice that the trunks of the trees grow closer here, their entwined branches all but blotting out the sky.  While it is difficult to see very far in any direction, you can discern some light to the northeast."],"exits":[{"to":341,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":344,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":344,"x":-180,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Meek","descriptions":["The ground is rocky and uneven as it rises up the base of the Siergelde.  Large insects bred in the moist earth buzz about your feet and near your face as you move cautiously through the darkness.  A faint shimmer of light dances like a mirage to the southwest."],"exits":[{"to":343,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":345,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":345,"x":-200,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Meek","descriptions":["Moss clings heavily to the tree trunks and rocks within this forest grove.  The ground is springy beneath your feet as you make your way through the near darkness.  You can hear the occasional screech of a ringed owl breaking through the thick air, mingled with the constant buzz of insects.  The trees appear to thin to the southwest."],"exits":[{"to":344,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":346,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":346,"x":-220,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Meek","descriptions":["A heavy breeze stirs the canopy of the forest grove, and the parted branches reveal patches of sky.  Freshly-fallen leaves mix with damp soil to create a pleasant, earthy scent."],"exits":[{"to":345,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":347,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":347,"x":-200,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Regard","descriptions":["Here at the base of the Siergelde, a sheer drop of exposed rock rises from the thick forest grove.  Soft light filters through the open air between the rockface and the canopy of the grove, causing the rock to glisten as if flecked with tiny pieces of glass.  A cool, wispy breeze occasionally wends by, breaking the humidity.","Here at the base of the Siergelde, a sheer drop of exposed rock rises from the thick forest grove.  Soft moonlight filters through the open air between the rockface and the canopy of the grove, causing the rock to glisten as if flecked with tiny pieces of glass.  A cool, wispy breeze occasionally wends by, breaking the humidity."],"exits":[{"to":346,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":348,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":348,"x":-200,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Regard","descriptions":["Your breath catches in your throat as you make your way carefully along the steep rockface.  An occasional bromeliad peeks out from a narrow crevice, its bright color commanding your attention."],"exits":[{"to":349,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":347,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":349,"x":-200,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Regard","descriptions":["The view from this point of the rocky incline is awe-inspiring.  Beyond the treetops of the forest which skirts the hillside, you can see grassy plains spreading east to west, and far to the north, another forested area that appears to follow a high town wall.  The air is particularly crisp, as if charged with energy."],"exits":[{"to":351,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":350,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":348,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":350,"x":-220,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Regard","descriptions":["Light green grasses envelope the hillside, which rises sharply to its top from where you stand.  Little tufts of white, spindly flowers wave back and forth in the breeze like flimsy porcelain bells.  Dark stones seem to peek at you from around the hill, and a worn trail has been deeply cut along the sharp incline to the summit."],"exits":[{"to":349,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":352,"exit":"go","move":"go trail"}]},
  {"id":351,"x":-180,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Regard","descriptions":["A gentle bluff provides a restful place to breathe the sweet, clean air of the hillside.  Far beyond the trees that mark the perimeter of the town walls to the north, you can see jagged peaks jutting into thick bands of clouds at the horizon."],"exits":[{"to":349,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":352,"x":-220,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde's Regard","descriptions":["The remnant of an incredible building surrounds the summit of the hill.  Two great juniper trees grow straight into the sky on either side of a massive archway that stretches across the width of the trail.  Through the archway, you can see that some of the original architecture remains standing, though most of the outer walls of the building have crumbled to nothing.  A stillness broken only by the whisper of the wind envelopes the area."],"exits":[{"to":350,"exit":"go","move":"go worn trail"},{"to":353,"exit":"go","move":"go massive archway"}]},
  {"id":353,"x":-180,"y":380,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["A carpet of thick rolling grasses is punctuated by tiny lavender flowers in what looks to be the foyer of the building.  A great monolith of speckled granite towers above you, its midsection etched with images.  Sparse tufts of juriweed skirt the point where the monolith has been driven into the ground by a power greater than any you can imagine."],"exits":[{"to":354,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":361,"exit":"go","move":"go stones"},{"to":352,"exit":"go","move":"go massive archway"}]},
  {"id":354,"x":-160,"y":400,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["A jagged stone has fallen from the top of the ruin walls and lies in the center of a massive arch.  A clump of juriweed has rooted beneath it, sending long spindly stems out in all directions.  Through the archway, you can clearly see the grasslands below, hemmed at the horizon by a thickly-wooded forest.  You notice there is little sound save the whisper of the wind."],"exits":[{"to":355,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":353,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":355,"x":-160,"y":420,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["A large statue rises from the midst of a short crop of bushes near a crumbling archway.  Clinging vines rooted deeply in the ancient mortar snake their way up the massive column stones, straining to reach the ornate architrave.  Upon the architrave are carved various fruits, flowers and grains which surround a weathered brass plaque.  The short, sweet song of a meadow lark reaches your ears, breaking the deep silence."],"exits":[{"to":354,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":356,"exit":"go","move":"go crumbling archway"}]},
  {"id":356,"x":-180,"y":440,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["A collapsed retaining wall of dark stones provides stark contrast to the lush green grasses.  Light filters through ragged cracks in the wall, creating a lacy shadow on the ground.  Part of a crumbled frieze lies nearby, upon which sits a weather-worn statuette.  Through a west-facing archway, you can see a tiny grove of trees standing serenely near what seems to be a broken monolith."],"exits":[{"to":357,"exit":"go","move":"go west-facing archway"},{"to":355,"exit":"go","move":"go crumbling archway"}]},
  {"id":357,"x":-220,"y":440,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["A sparse grove of trees stands just beyond an elliptical arch in the ruins.  Abutting the trees are two massive black stones, each as long as a two-story building is high.  They lie crookedly in the grass, overlapping each other like two snuggling giants.  This broken monolith once stood as a single piece, a mighty landmark that would have been visible from the grassland below.  On closer inspection, you note there are images painted on them."],"exits":[{"to":358,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":356,"exit":"go","move":"go elliptical arch"}]},
  {"id":358,"x":-240,"y":420,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["Bright buttercups grow in tight patches along this edge of the ruin.  A support column has collapsed, tumbling the massive building stones into a great pile.  In front of this pile are three jagged rocks driven partially into the ground, forming a semi-circle.  Some previous visitor has painted images and symbols upon these rocks in a white, chalky substance that has nearly worn away."],"exits":[{"to":359,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":357,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":359,"x":-240,"y":400,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["Chips of white granite are strewn across the hillside, mixed with the dark stones of the ruins.  A large section of a carved architrave lies on the grass, overgrown with woodrose vines and worn by the elements.  Here and there, a patch of wildflowers has taken root among the stones."],"exits":[{"to":360,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":358,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":360,"x":-220,"y":380,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Ruins","descriptions":["The gentle slope of the hillside is littered with dark, well-hewn stones and tiny lavender flowers.  A massive sculpture appears to sink at an angle into the ground, surrounded by tufts of wildflowers.  From this vantage point, you can see the canopy of the forest which skirts the base of this hill.  A gentle breeze envelopes you, instilling a sense of peace and tranquility."],"exits":[{"to":359,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":361,"exit":"go","move":"go stones"},{"to":362,"exit":"go","move":"go meandering path"}]},
  {"id":361,"x":-200,"y":380,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, Stone Grotto","descriptions":["Some of the building stones from the ruins that surround you have been fashioned into a shallow grotto at the very top of this hill.  Within the grotto, four rounded stones of descending size are set one upon the other in the manner of a crude altar.  At the foot of this altar, you find fruits and flowers in various stages of decay, the remnants of offerings to whatever power pervades this quietly sacred site."],"exits":[{"to":353,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":360,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#800080","aliases":["Siergelde","Favors"]},
  {"id":362,"x":-180,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde, High Path","descriptions":["The lush grass of the hillside gives way to rockier terrain as this meandering dirt path approaches what looks like open air.  Though a thick copse obscures the view in the westward direction, a vista of browns and greens spreads onward to the west, sometimes accented by a touch of crimson the further it stretches."],"exits":[{"to":363,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":363,"x":-20,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["Chill wind whips from the bluffs below this ancient path, which is overgrown with weeds and pitted with holes.  Hugging desperately at the very edge of the cliff, the pebbled walkway provides an incredible view of the lands far below -- lush, green and inviting, stretching for miles.  Something akin to the song of a thrush drifts liltingly by.","Chill wind whips from the bluffs below this ancient path, which is overgrown with weeds and pitted with holes.  Desperately hugging the edge of the cliff, the pebbled walkway wends along with no hint of beginning or end.  Only a stark black border, where all the stars have fled, marks the land which stretches on and on, far below the rambling precipice."],"exits":[{"to":364,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":360,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":364,"x":-20,"y":360,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["Loose pebbles fall away from the cliff to click and clack until they reach the obscurity of the world below.  While the rest of the promontory is carpeted by flat grasses, the trodden seam is home to rugged tufts of juriweed.  These hearty plants grow in forms suggesting dancers twirling merrily in fancy skirts."],"exits":[{"to":363,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":365,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":365,"x":-40,"y":380,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["A slight dip in the path signals a narrowing of the trail.  The land tilts steeply toward the empty air, and is traversable only with extreme caution.  Further south, it turns sharply and seems to disappear."],"exits":[{"to":364,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":366,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":366,"x":-60,"y":400,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["From this vantage point, the deep crimson walls of the cliffs are visible as they plummet to the land below.  Their delicate, chalky appearance offers little confidence to those who prefer firmer ground.  Deep, vertical ruts give the impression of these cliffs being forced up from the world below, by an impressively strong -- or extremely angry -- godlike being."],"exits":[{"to":365,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":367,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":367,"x":-60,"y":420,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["A large boulder with a massive crack through its middle, sits at this bend in the path.  The horrifying thing about it is that each mighty surge of wind sets it to shimmying ever so slightly.  It is unclear how many years this ungainly thing has perched in this place, and it is equally unclear where it came from, since its sparkling obsidian exterior looks nothing like the remainder of the area."],"exits":[{"to":366,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":368,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":368,"x":-80,"y":440,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["Large chunks of path have slipped a few inches down the cliff, and the only things holding them in place are the weeds.  As the cliff inclines, a ledge of rock forms between the pathway and the void beyond, and the ground is interspersed with cheerful yellow dirdel."],"exits":[{"to":367,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":369,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":369,"x":-100,"y":460,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["A dead tree juts out of the ledge along the cliff, its lifeless form suspended by its complex root system.  Wind, screeching up toward the path, sets it to bobbing now and again, making it seem like its gnarled lower branch is pointing insistently at the land below."],"exits":[{"to":368,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":370,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":370,"x":-100,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["An abrupt change in land level forces one to climb in order to make further progress.  Chalky red dirt flies loosely in the wind, settling thickly on exposed skin and clothing."],"exits":[{"to":369,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":371,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rise"}]},
  {"id":371,"x":-80,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, High Path","descriptions":["Southward, the landscape is crossed by a sharply twisting ribbon of eroded soil which is the remnant of a primeval river.  Its curves snake dangerously close to the edge of the cliffs before they disappear completely in a far-off forest.  To the north, by contrast, all one can see is grassland sitting upon the deep red chalk of the cliff's face."],"exits":[{"to":372,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":370,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rise"}]},
  {"id":372,"x":-100,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The deep grasses which line this portion of the cliff's only trail are heavily trodden but nontheless resilient.  Their bruised blades follow the course of the dried-up river as it cuts its way along the cliff."],"exits":[{"to":371,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":373,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":373,"x":-80,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":374,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":372,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":374,"x":-60,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":373,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":375,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":375,"x":-40,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":376,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":374,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":376,"x":-20,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":377,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":375,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":377,"x":0,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":378,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":376,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":378,"x":20,"y":500,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":379,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":377,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":379,"x":40,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":380,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":378,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":380,"x":60,"y":460,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":379,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":381,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":381,"x":80,"y":440,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":382,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":380,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":382,"x":80,"y":420,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":383,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":381,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":383,"x":80,"y":400,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":384,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":382,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":384,"x":80,"y":380,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":383,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":385,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":385,"x":80,"y":360,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":384,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":386,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":386,"x":60,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":385,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":387,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":387,"x":40,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":386,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":388,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":388,"x":20,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":387,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":389,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":389,"x":0,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":388,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":390,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":390,"x":-10,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":389,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":391,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":391,"x":-20,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":390,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":392,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":392,"x":-30,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":391,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":393,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":393,"x":-40,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":392,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":394,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":394,"x":-50,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":393,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":395,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":395,"x":-60,"y":300,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":394,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":396,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":396,"x":-80,"y":280,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":397,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":395,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":397,"x":-100,"y":260,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":398,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":396,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":398,"x":-120,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":402,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":397,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":399,"x":-140,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":400,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":402,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":400,"x":-140,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":401,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":399,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":401,"x":-120,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Great Break","descriptions":["A sudden break in the cliffs prohibits any further travel.  Known as the Great Break, this jagged rift separates the southern end of the riverbed from its northern part.  Far down at the bottom of the Great Break is a landscape of treetops, and the hint of a small lake.  Beyond it, the riverbed continues its winding course into a dusty, far-off horizon."],"exits":[{"to":400,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":402,"x":-140,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Siergelde Cliffs, Meander","descriptions":["The riverbed continues its lazy maneuver over the landscape at the cliff's edge.  Clipped grasses spread along the outer edge of the path, but everything adjacent to the riverbed is dry and dusty."],"exits":[{"to":399,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":398,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":403,"x":-180,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Pear Tree, Canopy","descriptions":["The leafy treetop forms a secure if spongy carpet beneath you, fanning out in all directions like a shimmering umbrella.  Tantalizing vreeland pears hang just out of reach, golden brown and tempting.  You can climb down the way you came up, or rest here for a bit."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"climb","move":"climb pear tree"}]},
  {"id":404,"x":-640,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["A large bramble patch seems to block any hope of movement to the south.  In the thick loam beneath the trees a barely visible path heads northeast."],"exits":[{"to":405,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":114,"exit":"go","move":"go bramble patch"}]},
  {"id":405,"x":-620,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["The trees thin out a little here giving more light to the undergrowth.  Several clusters of bright red, sharp yellow and deep blue flowers help break up the green and brown monotony of the forest.  To the north through the tree tops some mountain peaks are barely visible."],"exits":[{"to":406,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":404,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":406,"x":-620,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["A jagged stump as large around as a table sticks dangerously out of the ground.  It looks as if a group of mad lumberjacks hacked at a tree with hand axes before the upper portion finally ripped away from the stump.  Leading from the stump, deep ruts in the ground head northeast."],"exits":[{"to":407,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":405,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":407,"x":-600,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["The path is marred with deep ruts which lead to the ragged end of a large felled tree.  Some of the tree's branches have gotten caught on the surrounding bushes preventing it from being dragged any further. Fortunately, the tree was shoved somewhat off the northern side of path giving barely enough room to continue northeast."],"exits":[{"to":408,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":406,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":409,"exit":"climb","move":"climb felled tree"}]},
  {"id":408,"x":-580,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["The path disappears here amid small bushes and tall trees.  High overhead, a battered hip boot swings casually in the wind apparently caught at the ankle by a snare.  More tripped, but empty snares dangle from various tree limbs, silent testimony to their makers lack of skill."],"exits":[{"to":407,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":482,"exit":"go","move":"search go trampled path"}]},
  {"id":409,"x":-620,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["A group of squirrels cavorts in the undergrowth and dry leaves.  Suddenly one of them dashes part way up a tree, only to be soundly chittered at by the others.  He dives down among them, rolling several end over end, before disappearing into a bush."],"exits":[{"to":410,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":407,"exit":"climb","move":"climb felled tree"}]},
  {"id":410,"x":-640,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["Nestled beneath some large ferns, an old lean-to offers a little protection from the elements.  In front of it, a well-used fire pit and a poorly hidden cache of fire wood suggests that there are frequent visitors here."],"exits":[{"to":409,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":411,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":411,"x":-660,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["Hundreds of bees fly in and out of this area, at times coming dangerously close.  Their activity seems to be centered around a hollowed trunk which they've converted into a Gor'tog-sized hive."],"exits":[{"to":410,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":412,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":412,"x":-680,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Deep Forest","descriptions":["To the north, the dense forest is interrupted by a dry creek bed running roughly east and west.  The edge of the creek has eroded creating a gentle slope down to the bed."],"exits":[{"to":411,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":413,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":413,"x":-660,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Dry Creek Bed","descriptions":["It's been some time since water has flowed through this creek bed.  The hollows and low points of the bed have filled with leaves and dirt.  The southern lip of the creek has eroded creating a gentle slope up."],"exits":[{"to":417,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":414,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":412,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":414,"x":-680,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Dry Creek Bed","descriptions":["In sharp contrast to the thriving forest to the north and south, a small, lanky flowering bush clings to life on the rocky bed.  Though sunlight is plentiful, there is barely enough soil or water to sustain it."],"exits":[{"to":413,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":415,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":415,"x":-700,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Dry Creek Bed","descriptions":["From the west, the sounds of flowing water and a flash of blue indicate that a river is close by.  The silt and sand partially covering the creek bed and a few small pockets of fresh water suggest that the river level sometimes raises enough to allow water up this far."],"exits":[{"to":414,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":416,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":416,"x":-720,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, River's Edge","descriptions":["A wide band of smooth rocks and pebbles runs between the placid river to the west and the dense forest to the east.  When the river is at its fullest, this area is probably underwater.  A couple of fishing poles have been propped up near the water's edge, their lines trailing far downstream."],"exits":[{"to":415,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":417,"x":-640,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Dry Creek Bed","descriptions":["Completely oblivious to any other activity, a pair of ravens argue over a single shiny rock embedded in the creek bed.  At various times, each one manages to land briefly and work at prying the stone loose before the other swoops down and knocks its competitor away."],"exits":[{"to":418,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":413,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":418,"x":-620,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Dry Creek Bed","descriptions":["Dusty footprints weave back and forth between the banks of the creek bed.  The partly exposed roots of a tree up on the north bank serve as a reminder that once water flowed swiftly through here."],"exits":[{"to":419,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":417,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":424,"exit":"climb","move":"climb tree roots"}]},
  {"id":419,"x":-600,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest Fen","descriptions":["The ground slopes abruptly down from the creek bed into a small fen.  Once a large pond, a slow decrease in water has allowed marsh grasses and flowers to flourish.  The sounds of crickets and frogs fill the air with a pleasant melody."],"exits":[{"to":422,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":423,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":420,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":418,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":420,"x":-580,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest Fen","descriptions":["The foul smell of long standing water and decaying plants fills the air.  A boot lies half buried in the thick, goopy mud that covers the area.  To the north, a mountain range looms over the tree tops."],"exits":[{"to":423,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":421,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":419,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":421,"x":-560,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest Fen","descriptions":["The remnants of a beaver dam occupy much of this area.  Marsh grasses and a few small bushes push up through the graying tangle of tree branches and sapling trunks.  Amid the wreckage are signs of bird nests and small animal burrows."],"exits":[{"to":420,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":423,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":422,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":422,"x":-580,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest Fen","descriptions":["The forest to the north is eagerly encroaching on the marsh grasses and flowers.  Several young saplings compete for sunlight and air with a variety of bushes."],"exits":[{"to":421,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":423,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":419,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":423,"x":-580,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest Fen","descriptions":["A shallow algae-filled pond occupies the center of this area.  Dragonflies buzz around, darting up and down over the water before disappearing amid the tall marsh grass.  To the north, the upper peaks of the mountains can barely be seen above the forest."],"exits":[{"to":422,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":421,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":420,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":419,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":424,"x":-640,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["A high bank overlooks the dry creek bed to the south. At some point the bank eroded, partially exposing the roots of a tall satinwood.  When the breeze tugs at the tree's upper canopy, the tree creaks ominously and the ground shudders slightly."],"exits":[{"to":425,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":418,"exit":"climb","move":"climb tree roots"}]},
  {"id":425,"x":-640,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["The air is heavy with the vanilla-sweet smell of some flowering bushes that cover the area.  Hummingbirds dart among the pale yellow flowers, stopping now and again for a sip of nectar."],"exits":[{"to":426,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":424,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":426,"x":-620,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["The trees line both sides of the path, arching together to form a mottled green canopy overhead that looks more like the ceiling of an elaborate temple.  Flowers and ferns carpet the area beneath the trees."],"exits":[{"to":427,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":425,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":427,"x":-600,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["A few blackened tree trunks stand in a large burned out area.  The tallest among them has been split in two apparently by a lightning bolt.  Half the trunk remains standing while the other half lies twisted and scarred among the burned out undergrowth."],"exits":[{"to":428,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":426,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":428,"x":-600,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["A large wilted bramble bush looks oddly out of place among the ferns and satinwood trees in the area.  Even more odd, what looks like its roots, still partially covered in dirt, stick out from the top of the bush."],"exits":[{"to":429,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":427,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":430,"exit":"go","move":"go wilted bush"}]},
  {"id":429,"x":-580,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["The path ends suddenly in a large pit.  Part of the pit is covered by a motley arrangement of tree branches barely concealed by a thin layer of dirt, leaves, and uprooted bushes.  At the bottom of the pit, sharpened poles and jagged edged rocks point ominously upwards."],"exits":[{"to":428,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":430,"x":-620,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["The southern end of the path disappears abruptly under a large wilted bramble bush.  A few shriveled berries and flowers still cling to the bush.  Around it, the other vegetation grows strong and lush beneath the satinwood trees."],"exits":[{"to":431,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":428,"exit":"go","move":"go wilted bush"}]},
  {"id":431,"x":-640,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["Bramble bushes compete with cinnamon ferns for light and space between the trees.  Something has been helping the ferns along by ripping out and discarding some of the larger bushes."],"exits":[{"to":432,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":430,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":432,"x":-640,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["The tall trees thin out, allowing the mountain range to the north to come suddenly into view.  In the forefront a long ridge heads sharply up towards the closest peak.  In the far distance to the east, the top of a smoking volcano can barely be seen."],"exits":[{"to":431,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":433,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":433,"x":-660,"y":-340,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["Crude drawings of hunts, battles, and weapons cover a large outcropping of rocks.  Those drawn with chalk or paint are faded and partially gone, while others, carved into the surface, seemed destined to last forever."],"exits":[{"to":432,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":434,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":436,"exit":"go","move":"go large outcropping"}]},
  {"id":434,"x":-680,"y":-340,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["A loud crashing and thrashing from the bushes startles you.  Suddenly, several deer come leaping across the area.  In the distance can be heard a cougar's snarl, then an all too-brief bleating."],"exits":[{"to":433,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":435,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":435,"x":-700,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Forest","descriptions":["The path again disappears as the bushes and other undergrowth close in beneath the trees."],"exits":[{"to":434,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":436,"x":-640,"y":-340,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The rocky outcropping contains a small pocket of fresh water.  Around the water, bold red and creamy white lilies flourish.  Tracks of animals large and small can be seen in the mud at the water's edge."],"exits":[{"to":437,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":433,"exit":"go","move":"go large outcropping"}]},
  {"id":437,"x":-620,"y":-360,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The path threads its way through, over, and around large rocks and boulders.  If it weren't for the looming ridge to the north, it would be difficult to keep track of directions."],"exits":[{"to":438,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":436,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":438,"x":-600,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["Part of the ridge has given way, partially covering the path.  A wedge of land slid down the side a little way, leaving the trees and bushes in the wedge still standing, while those at the edge lean precariously at different angles."],"exits":[{"to":439,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":437,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":439,"x":-580,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The path turns sharply here heading to either side of the ridge.  On a small hill to the northeast, a couple of large figures seem to be observing the path from a look-out platform built among the trees."],"exits":[{"to":438,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":440,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":440,"x":-600,"y":-420,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The ridge is not very steep here, but dense undergrowth still prevents anyone from climbing it.  The trees are not as tall or as dense as in the lower forest, but there are still satinwoods and oaks mixed in with redbuds and dogwoods."],"exits":[{"to":439,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":441,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":441,"x":-620,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The path begins to slip away from the ridge towards a small valley nestled between the mountains.  In the distance, a couple of smoke plumes rise above the forest before dissipating in the wind."],"exits":[{"to":442,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":440,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":442,"x":-620,"y":-460,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["There is a rustling sound in the undergrowth beyond a fallen tree.  Suddenly, up pops a squirrel.  He climbs up on the tree, stares around for a bit, then starts licking and cleaning his fur, pausing only to sniff at a tree beetle crawling nearby."],"exits":[{"to":441,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":443,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#C2B280","aliases":["RTZ15","RT-KC-K"]},
  {"id":443,"x":-640,"y":-480,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["An old wooden fence blocks the path continuing west.  A half-open gate barely hangs on a post with a couple of shredded leather hinges.  A gust of wind or a swift kick would probably knock the whole thing over."],"exits":[{"to":442,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":444,"exit":"go","move":"go half-open gate"}]},
  {"id":444,"x":-680,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The path crosses a large grassy clearing with a few scattered fire pits.  Off to one side, the bed of a wagon lies abandoned on the ground.  A broken axle and a couple of wheels are half-hidden in the taller grass nearby."],"exits":[{"to":445,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":443,"exit":"go","move":"go half-open gate"}]},
  {"id":445,"x":-700,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["Crickets and katydids fill the air with a hushed drone.  Occasionally, the muted hoots of owls and the flapping of wings break the sleepy peace of the forest night.  ","The chirping and chattering of hundreds of sparrows in the trees above is almost deafening.  Startled by something making noise in the bushes below, they suddenly take wing.  In several large groups, they fly in and around the trees before settling back down."],"exits":[{"to":444,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":446,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":446,"x":-720,"y":-460,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Sparse Forest","descriptions":["The trees and undergrowth are so thick that little can be seen beyond the faint path.  Ivy has grown at least part way up most of the trees, and sometimes between them, forming living veils."],"exits":[{"to":447,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":445,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":447,"x":-720,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Gully","descriptions":["An occasional glimpse of distant peaks can be caught through the leafy canopy to the north.  The sounds of birdsong are muted, with only a faint melody breaking the silence.  A dry streambed cuts across the forest floor, spanned by an old rope bridge that sways gently in the breeze."],"exits":[{"to":448,"exit":"go","move":"go rope bridge"},{"to":446,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#C2B280","aliases":["RTZ14","RT-KC-XW"]},
  {"id":448,"x":-720,"y":-540,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Rope Bridge","descriptions":["The bridge creaks ominously underfoot.  Jagged rocks fill the gully below, waiting for anyone foolish enough to tempt fate.  Rolling hills are evident to the north, while a wall of trees presents itself south of the bridge."],"exits":[{"to":449,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":447,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":449,"x":-720,"y":-560,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Sentry","descriptions":["A lone Gor'Tog stands motionless, his dark leathers rendering him almost indistinguishable from the surrounding underbrush.  The sentry's eyes scan constantly for signs of danger, the slightest movement instantly drawing his attention.  A low wooden building can be glimpsed off to the west, while to the north the thinning forest gives way to hills.  A rope bridge spans a dry gully south of here."],"exits":[{"to":452,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":450,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":448,"exit":"go","move":"go rope bridge"}],"color":"#808000","aliases":["Knife Clan","Kraelyst start point","travel start point"]},
  {"id":450,"x":-740,"y":-560,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Wooden Shack","descriptions":["An array of weaponry, mostly clubs and spears, lean against the side of a dilapidated shack.  Muffled thumps from inside betray the presence of at least one occupant."],"exits":[{"to":449,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":451,"exit":"go","move":"go dilapidated shack"}]},
  {"id":451,"x":-740,"y":-580,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Old Shack","descriptions":["Sagging cots are strewn about this tiny shack.  Off duty sentries catch a few precious moments of sleep while they await their shifts.  Only a few of the mattresses are presently occupied, but the sheer bulk of the slumbering guards is impressive."],"exits":[{"to":450,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":452,"x":-720,"y":-580,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["This beaten dirt path threads its way over lightly wooded hills.  Outskirts of a small settlement can barely be made out to the north, against the backdrop of jagged peaks."],"exits":[{"to":453,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":449,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#C2B280","aliases":["Ranger Cache","Cache","RTZCache","RT-KC-KCCR"]},
  {"id":453,"x":-720,"y":-600,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Several fierce-looking Gor'Togs loiter about the entrance to a small cave.  Dressed in brightly dyed leathers and carrying an impressive amount of weaponry, the Gor'Togs appear ready for battle at a moment's notice.  The crackling of an open fire to the east fills the air."],"exits":[{"to":458,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":459,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":456,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":452,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":454,"exit":"go","move":"go small cave"}]},
  {"id":454,"x":-740,"y":-600,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Bukor's Leatherworks","descriptions":["Low tables are pushed up against bare rock walls in this natural cavern.  Carefully tanned furs and leathers are arranged haphazardly about the area, no thought having been given to a proper display.  Bukor, a Gor'Tog of great skill but suspect taste, is well known in the Clan for his temper.  He knows his work is excellent, and expects to be compensated accordingly."],"exits":[{"to":455,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":453,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Bukor's Leatherworks"]},
  {"id":455,"x":-720,"y":-620,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Back Room","descriptions":["A pine counter liberally spattered with a muddied rainbow of colors blocks passage deeper into the room.  Near a dark curtain at the back of the shop can be seen several barrels of pigmented metallic powders stacked carelessly next to a large bucket of half-dried paint.  Klurge, the proprieter of the operation, stands behind the counter, watching incoming customers with suspicious eyes.  A color menu list is nailed to the wall to the left of the exit."],"exits":[{"to":454,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Dyer","Klurge"]},
  {"id":456,"x":-700,"y":-580,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Woodland's Edge","descriptions":["Rolling hills give way to wooded plains, the sounds of the forest a welcome relief from the bustle of the Gor'Tog settlement to the north.  A beaten dirt path, worn from years of heavy use, leads deeper into the primeval wood."],"exits":[{"to":459,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":457,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":453,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":466,"exit":"go","move":"go dirt path"}]},
  {"id":457,"x":-680,"y":-600,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Woodland's Edge","descriptions":["Wooden buildings, a rare sight among the many cave dwellings, huddle about a clear pond.  Though unadorned, their construction seems sound enough.  Fingers of grey smoke curl into the air from the top of an unobtrusive shop."],"exits":[{"to":460,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":456,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":459,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":458,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":465,"exit":"go","move":"go unobtrusive shop"},{"to":526,"exit":"go","move":"go winding path"}]},
  {"id":458,"x":-700,"y":-620,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Caves honeycomb the rocky hills, providing shelter from the elements for the many warriors who inhabit the area.  Gor'Togs cluster about, yelling to one another in booming shouts.  Boisterous laughter splits the air, its origin impossible to determine.  One particularly large cave entrance draws the eye."],"exits":[{"to":457,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":459,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":453,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":461,"exit":"go","move":"go cave entrance"}]},
  {"id":459,"x":-700,"y":-600,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Firepit","descriptions":["Scorching heat rises from a roaring bonfire at the center of this sandy pit.  A huge boar slowly rotates over the fire, sending the scent of burnt flesh wafting into the air.  An elderly Gor'Tog, immensely strong despite his years, turns the spit with a steady rhythm."],"exits":[{"to":458,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":457,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":456,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":453,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Firepit"]},
  {"id":460,"x":-660,"y":-620,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Towering mountains block out the sky and create a natural barrier protecting the Clan's flank.  A wrought-iron gate, undoubtedly imposing in any other setting, pales in comparison.  The portal seems oddly out of place amidst the rocky crags."],"exits":[{"to":457,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":461,"x":-700,"y":-640,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Cavern","descriptions":["By far the largest cavern in Trefan Iltesh, this vast cave serves as both a central meeting place and, more frequently, as a giant arena.  Opponents square off in the middle of a roughly circular pit carved into the rocky floor while onlookers gather about the edge and hurl insults or cheers as their champions' fortunes change.  Smaller caverns breaking off from the main cave lead in several directions."],"exits":[{"to":463,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":462,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":458,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":464,"exit":"go","move":"go small cavern"}]},
  {"id":462,"x":-680,"y":-640,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Cavern","descriptions":["The sharp CRACK! of clashing weaponry echoes madly through this rocky chamber.  Almost palpable waves of heat roll off grim-faced Gor'Togs as they flail at one another in preparation for their trials in the arena.  Despite their bulk, opponents dance nimbly through the natural obstacles formed by thrusting stalagmites.  A few heavy boulders have been pushed into one corner of the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":461,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":463,"x":-700,"y":-660,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Shrine","descriptions":["The dim light from a few flickering torches is not enough to cut through the gloom that pervades this cramped alcove.  The cold stone walls seem to close in on all sides.  Against the far wall leans a carved granite statue of a fierce weasel, its small size oddly out of place among the giant Gor'Togs that inhabit these caves."],"exits":[{"to":461,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Shrine","Huldah"]},
  {"id":464,"x":-720,"y":-640,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Healer's Kitchen","descriptions":["The cramped room smells of baked goods with fading notes of an antiseptic.  Standing torches illuminate the whitewashed floor and matching stone walls.  Darker stains can be seen beyond the coating of both, a testament to the lifetime of surgeries and triage that were once performed here.  Now, the sounds of such medicine are replaced with the rhythmic pounding of herbs in mortars and stirring of medicines and batters in large bowls.","Whitewashed floors and stone walls barely conceal darker stains beneath.  The sounds of remedy preparation and smells of baking dominate the space."],"exits":[{"to":461,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Healer's Kitchen","herb shop","Dokt"]},
  {"id":465,"x":-660,"y":-600,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Tobb's Smithy","descriptions":["Knives of all shapes, sizes, and descriptions occupy every available surface in this tiny shop.  Care must be taken to avoid any sudden movement, or painful consequences may result.  But despite the eccentricity of his establishment, Tobb the smith is almost revered by his patrons for the detailed craftsmanship with which he goes about his work."],"exits":[{"to":457,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Tobb's Smithy"]},
  {"id":466,"x":-700,"y":-540,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Woodland Trail","descriptions":["Gnarled branches claw at the air, and tangled roots seem intent on tripping the unwary.  The fresh spoor of large game is apparent, a sure sign of plentiful hunting.  A beaten dirt path leads back to the settlement."],"exits":[{"to":467,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":456,"exit":"go","move":"go dirt path"}]},
  {"id":467,"x":-680,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Primeval Glade","descriptions":["A circular clearing has been carved out of the dense wood, the lumber apparently used to construct the cabin that fills most of this break in the forest.  Constant battle is obviously waged to prevent the surrounding underbrush from encroaching into the area."],"exits":[{"to":471,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":470,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":469,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":468,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":466,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"aliases":["Primeval Glade"]},
  {"id":468,"x":-700,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Woodlands","descriptions":["The wind lends a biting chill to the air as it whips through the trees.  An eerie whistling originates from some oddly-shaped reeds.  Perhaps because of the sound, wildlife seems to avoid this area."],"exits":[{"to":467,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":469,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":469,"x":-680,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Woodlands","descriptions":["Ancient trees soar skyward here in the heart of the primeval forest.  The mammoth trunks dwarf even the Gor'Tog hunters that frequent the glade in search of game.  One blackened stump pays testament to the violent storms that sometimes frequent these lands."],"exits":[{"to":467,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":471,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":470,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":468,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#C2B280","aliases":["RTZ16","RT-KC-HF"]},
  {"id":470,"x":-660,"y":-500,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Deep Forest's Edge","descriptions":["Pale grey mosses grow in curtains among clustered trees.  A black squirrel chirrs happily to himself as he scampers across an overhead limb.  With a heroic leap, the squirrel hurls himself through the air, only to land triumphantly moments later on a distant branch."],"exits":[{"to":471,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":469,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":467,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":471,"x":-660,"y":-520,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Deep Forest's Edge","descriptions":["A few taffelberry bushes have managed to find a niche here in the shadow of looming trees.  From the bushes' rather barren appearance, the local wildlife has acquired quite a taste for the sweet berries."],"exits":[{"to":470,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":469,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":467,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":472,"x":-80,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Tower West, Air Floor","descriptions":["A dark grey carpet decorated with a pattern of crossing black lightning bolts covers the floor, matching the decoration on the grey-painted walls.  A constant, low thrum hangs just inside the range of hearing, its source nearby but not readily apparent.  Doors spaced in an even circle around the perimeter lead to initiates' private cells."],"exits":[{"to":473,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":5,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":476,"exit":"climb","move":"climb jade staircase"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Tower West","jade tower"]},
  {"id":473,"x":-80,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Tower West, Water Floor","descriptions":["Deep blue carpeting covers the floor, its surface cut in a manner that suggests the rippling of waves upon the surface of a lake.  Bright blue spirals, representing the element of water, fill the walls between a series of doors leading to initiates' private cells.  The air here is moist and cool upon the skin."],"exits":[{"to":474,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":472,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":474,"x":-80,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Tower West, Fire Floor","descriptions":["Lush, red carpeting covers the floor, muffling any ambient noise into oblivion.  Images of bloated red suns, representing the element of fire, fill the walls between a series of doors leading to initiates' private cells.  The air here is significantly warmer than on the tower's other floors, although the reason is not readily apparent."],"exits":[{"to":475,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":473,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":475,"x":-80,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Tower West, Aether Floor","descriptions":["Carpeting the color of a death shroud covers the floor, devouring the light as hungrily as Aldauth consumes souls.  The walls are devoid of decoration, instead painted a uniform black to match the floor.  Only the doors leading to initiates' cells betray any hint of color in this otherwise cold, bleak room."],"exits":[{"to":474,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":476,"x":-60,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Tower West, Earth Floor","descriptions":["Bare, dark soil forms the floor underfoot.  The stony walls surrounding this circular room are similarly devoid of decoration, keeping instead the plain, natural look preferred by those mages who favor the element of Earth.  Doors leading to the initiates' private cells line the walls."],"exits":[{"to":472,"exit":"climb","move":"climb jade staircase"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":477,"x":-780,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Arnack's Tavern, Bar Room","descriptions":["At first glimpse, the tavern offers all the sign outside promises.  In one corner, a pair of aged men play instruments and sing the occasional tune, while the other side of the room holds a number of tables and chairs for comfort and conversation.  Several patrons cluster around a dartboard on the back wall.  A barkeep bustles around behind a bar, barking at servers to hustle while keeping a welcoming smile for all the customers at the same time."],"exits":[{"to":128,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":478,"exit":"go","move":"go private room"},{"to":533,"exit":"south","move":""}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Arnack's Tavern"]},
  {"id":478,"x":-800,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Arnack's Tavern, Private Room","descriptions":["A table sits in the middle of this small room, surrounded by cushioned chairs.  A window in the back wall looks into the forest, limbs occasionally knocking against the glass with the sway of the wind.  The bustle of the main room is mostly muffled here allowing quiet and privacy if needed."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":479,"x":-780,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Chasm","descriptions":["Although cramped, this chasm connects two hollows and allows rainwater to flow away from the tiny oasis to the north.  Tiny pools of water dot the sandy floor.  Numerous large footprints almost obscure the dry runnels linking the puddles."],"exits":[{"to":480,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":481,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":480,"x":-780,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Hollow","descriptions":["This small hollow in the stone of the outcrop is surprisingly pleasant.  Dry rivulets in the ground suggest that rainwater carries loose dirt from higher on the mound and deposits it here, creating an oasis of both soil and water.  A variety of plants grow in this place -- little yellow bell-shaped flowers, puffy white ones, and tiny purple ones that grow scattered amongst all the others.  A vine with shiny leaves climbs up the walls, softening the otherwise harsh contours of the stone."],"exits":[{"to":479,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":333,"exit":"climb","move":"climb twisted vine"}]},
  {"id":481,"x":-760,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Rocky Outcrop, Hollow","descriptions":["Lush vines climb the sheer walls, growing up out of the deep pool that collects much of the runoff from the rocks above.  No exits exist but the one entrance, with the sheer rockface allowing no escape.  A litter of dried leaves and other debris lies scattered on the sandy ground."],"exits":[{"to":479,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":482,"x":-540,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Wilderness, Aberro Valley","descriptions":["Disappearing among the thick bushes and underbrush in the south, the trail north winds through the forest.  Pressed leaves and snapped twigs litter the ground, evidence of heavy use."],"exits":[{"to":483,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":408,"exit":"go","move":"go trampled path"}]},
  {"id":483,"x":-520,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Trampled Path","descriptions":["Twisting and turning through the trees, the meandering turns of the beaten track hinder visibility in all directions.  The sound of a nearby river filters through the dense trees."],"exits":[{"to":485,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":484,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":482,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":484,"x":-540,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Trampled Path","descriptions":["Skimming through the area on the west, a narrow river draws the local wildlife to it.  The chirrups of birds and various other animal noises can be discerned accompanying the flash of movement along the river's bank."],"exits":[{"to":483,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":485,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":486,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":485,"x":-520,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Trampled Path","descriptions":["Darkened beneath the dense trees, the forest sprawls across slowly sloping hills.  A fallen tree or two lean against those that still stand, as if unwilling to give up."],"exits":[{"to":483,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":486,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":484,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":486,"x":-540,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Trampled Path","descriptions":["Beginning to harden, the trail here grades into something more akin to gravel toward the south.  Several paths lead off into the darkened bosk, zigzagging through the woods."],"exits":[{"to":484,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":485,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":487,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":488,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":487,"x":-520,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["Laden with gravel, the trail becomes a climbing path, circling upwards and downwards on a hill within the large valley.  Trees and underbrush cling to life in the rocky ground, their sparse limbs stretching upwards."],"exits":[{"to":488,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":486,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":488,"x":-520,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["Upon the apex of a smaller hill, the trail here sketches itself deeper into the valley below on one side and rises steeply into a rocky track to the east.  Short grasses grow along the sides of the path, opening up into brief, truncated areas where a traveler may take a cautious rest."],"exits":[{"to":487,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":486,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":489,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rocky track"}]},
  {"id":489,"x":-500,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["Sparse vegetation dots the area here, leaving a precariously sloping path of gravel that winds its way through the valley.  In the distance, the calls of various creatures can be heard."],"exits":[{"to":490,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":492,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":491,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":488,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rocky track"}]},
  {"id":490,"x":-460,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["The parched landscape gives way to a rolling piedmont of hills that rise slowly upward toward a distant cliff face.  Low brush and sparse vegetation grows along the trail."],"exits":[{"to":493,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":492,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":489,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":491,"x":-500,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rock Slide","descriptions":["Large, jagged boulders jut upward from the ground like misaligned teeth, creating a macabre illusion of a lower jawbone across the hillside.  Patches of lichen and moss have wedged themselves betwixt the stones."],"exits":[{"to":489,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":492,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":492,"x":-480,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rock Slide","descriptions":["Despite the forests and greenery in the distance, in this elevated area of the valley, the air is arid and dusty.  Rock and gravel, stirred by passersby and animals, rise into the air, clogging it and giving it a gritty taste."],"exits":[{"to":490,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":491,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":489,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":493,"x":-460,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Growing in lushness, the underbrush here houses the occasional small creature that fills the air with sporadic sounds of movement.  Perhaps felled by a particularly strong storm, a large tree trunk lies adjacent to the path."],"exits":[{"to":495,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":494,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":490,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":494,"x":-420,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Barren Hillside","descriptions":["Cloistered near the cliff, a large dark hill rises in the distance, while the path towards the west slopes downward.  A small, stone well has been constructed here accompanied by the putrid smell of something long dead wafting from its depths."],"exits":[{"to":495,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":496,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":493,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":495,"x":-420,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Rolling Hills","descriptions":["Verdant abundance coats the hillside with a profusion of plants and small saplings.  Farther to the west, a sheer cliff wall rises upwards, marring the horizon with a dark, looming presence, as if something evil waited there."],"exits":[{"to":496,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":494,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":493,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":496,"x":-400,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Barren Hillside","descriptions":["Growing slippery, the once sturdy and grassy ground falls away to a consistently muddy surface in this area.  Looming against the horizon, the hulking mass of a dark cliff face rises upward."],"exits":[{"to":494,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":495,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":497,"exit":"climb","move":"climb muddy hill"}]},
  {"id":497,"x":-360,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Narrow Stream","descriptions":["Lush grass carpets the ground on the rocky slope.  Water seeps from the hillside, joining together into a small stream that flows to the west."],"exits":[{"to":498,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":499,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":496,"exit":"climb","move":"climb muddy hill"}]},
  {"id":498,"x":-380,"y":-220,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Narrow Stream","descriptions":["The small stream cascades down the slope, channeling a valley to the west.  Despite the nearby water, the surrounding brush is sparsely distributed across the hillside."],"exits":[{"to":499,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":497,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":500,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":499,"x":-380,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Narrow Stream","descriptions":["A deadfall dams part of the stream's path as it flows down the valley, creating a small pond.  Next to the pool, the remains of a campfire suggest that some traveler once used this space as a shelter."],"exits":[{"to":497,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":498,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":500,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":501,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":500,"x":-400,"y":-240,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Ravine","descriptions":["The banks of the stream continue to grow steeper and rockier.  Though the flow of water is still a mere trickle, over time this stream has made an impressive mark on the landscape."],"exits":[{"to":501,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":499,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":0,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":501,"x":-400,"y":-260,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Valley, Fetid Pool","descriptions":["As the stream takes a turn southward, the source of the stench becomes apparent.  The flow of water is blocked here by massive amounts of rotting refuse, causing the water to pool.  Bones, flesh, and rotting plants mingle with things less identifiable but more vile in a noxious soup.  To the north, a sheer cliff face rises upward."],"exits":[{"to":499,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":500,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":502,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff face"}]},
  {"id":502,"x":-400,"y":-280,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Cliffs, Above a Pool","descriptions":["Trees cling precariously to the cliff face, their leaves rustling in the blessedly fresh breeze.  The small stream below glistens in its ravine, sparkling and clear until its end at the putrid pool."],"exits":[{"to":501,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"},{"to":503,"exit":"climb","move":"climb up"}]},
  {"id":503,"x":-400,"y":-300,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Cliffs, Cliff Face","descriptions":["The trees here are more scraggly than those lower on the cliff face.  A dead sapling hangs unsteadily from a single remaining root.  Though unsuited to trees, the rocks do offer enough cracks and protrusions for climbing."],"exits":[{"to":502,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"},{"to":504,"exit":"climb","move":"climb up"}]},
  {"id":504,"x":-400,"y":-320,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Cliffs, Cliff Face","descriptions":["The rock face here is too sheer and solid for trees to take purchase, but tufts of tough grass sprout from occasional cracks.  Below, the specific features of the valley are lost in sea of green that is the forest."],"exits":[{"to":503,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"},{"to":505,"exit":"climb","move":"climb up"}]},
  {"id":505,"x":-400,"y":-340,"z":0,"title":"Aberro Cliffs, Beneath a Precipice","descriptions":["A narrow ledge offers respite from the grueling climb.  Above, the rock juts out sharply, providing some protection from the elements.  Just large enough to give a foothold, a small crack appears in the cliff face to the right of the overhang."],"exits":[{"to":504,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"},{"to":506,"exit":"climb","move":"climb crack"}]},
  {"id":506,"x":-400,"y":-360,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Cliff's Edge","descriptions":["A crude palisade assembled from assorted bones provides the last hand hold on the climb from the cliff face.  The palisade forms a semi-circle around the camp, but nothing guards the sheer drop over the cliff side.  Despite the perilous plunge, the precipice presents a commanding view."],"exits":[{"to":505,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff"},{"to":507,"exit":"go","move":"go faint pathway"}]},
  {"id":507,"x":-420,"y":-380,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Palisade","descriptions":["Assorted bones form a crude palisade, guarding the approach to the camp.  Nothing guards the sheer drop over the cliff side, where defenders could push potential invaders.  Darkness masks the difference between stone and air, making the drop more perilous."],"exits":[{"to":508,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":510,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":509,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":506,"exit":"go","move":"go faint pathway"}]},
  {"id":508,"x":-420,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Interior Sally Port","descriptions":["Just large enough to hold all occupants of the camp, forays into enemy territory launch from this location.  Debris litters the edges of this small gathering area."],"exits":[{"to":510,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":507,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":509,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":509,"x":-440,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Bivouac","descriptions":["Dismal tents sit low to the ground, providing small protection from the elements.  Noxious odors drift over from the latrine.  A small cedar tree clings to the mountainside just above the tents."],"exits":[{"to":511,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":512,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":508,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":507,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":510,"x":-400,"y":-400,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Firepit","descriptions":["Extinguished, the firepit houses burnt bones, meat, and gristle.  Suspended by a massive bone spit, an abomination waits for the cooks to finish roasting it.  The odor of the partially cooked meat smells rather like a latrine."],"exits":[{"to":512,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":507,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":508,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":511,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":511,"x":-440,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Command","descriptions":["This area doubles as housing for the commander and a briefing room.  The mountain encloses three sides of the area, while a tarp suspended from the stone provides shelter."],"exits":[{"to":510,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":509,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":512,"x":-400,"y":-440,"z":0,"title":"Xala'Shar Camp, Supplies","descriptions":["Empty crates litter the room, tossed in heaps once the quartermaster removed the contents.  The hinges on an open crate squeak as they sway in the wind."],"exits":[{"to":510,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":509,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":513,"x":-680,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"The Grove, Ancient Tree","descriptions":["Creaking limbs and branches intertwine to form a makeshift floor.  Within this airy landing, the cured hide of some long dead beast sways between two leafy boughs.  Scattered upon the floor, in several haphazard piles, lay mounds of various pelts.  Dangling from overhead like some macabre wind chime, a collection of skulls sways in the shifting breeze.","Several fireflies dart about the limbs and branches, lighting this airy landing.  An outline of a hide can be seen stretched between two branches.  Scattered along the floor are several lumpy mounds and a shadowy string of skulls hang from a nearby branch."],"exits":[{"to":104,"exit":"climb","move":"climb tree trunk"}],"aliases":["Food Tree"]},
  {"id":514,"x":-400,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Hunting Preserve, Woodpile","descriptions":["On top of this unsteady perch you have a view of the surrounding area.  Most directions are blocked by the heavy growth of trees, but the ruined chimneys of the manor poke above the treeline like broken teeth in a decaying mouth.  Not too far away, you catch a glimpse of the river that flows by the preserve."],"exits":[{"to":252,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":515,"x":-760,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan Home, Lodge Interior","descriptions":["The walls of the lodge are covered with the hides and skins of many different animals.  You recognize the pelts of otter, fox, deer and wolf.  Despite the spacious size of the lodge, the air in the windowless building is thick and hazy.  You can smell the residue of an aromatic, heavy smoke.  A large firepit in the center of the room is placed below the ceiling's smoke hole.  A massive rack attached to one wall holds enough weapons for a small army."],"exits":[{"to":131,"exit":"go","move":"go alcove"},{"to":516,"exit":"go","move":"go firepit"},{"to":517,"exit":"go","move":"go small doorway"}]},
  {"id":516,"x":-760,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan Home, Firepit","descriptions":["The air around the firepit is heavy with a sweet-smelling smoke.  A hole in the ceiling, directly above the pit, provides some relief with an occasional breeze.  Carved pipes and rattles made from gourds have been left on the dirt floor.  A tall barbarian warrior sits next to the fire, carefully attaching some eagle feathers to the end of a lance."],"exits":[{"to":515,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":517,"x":-780,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan Home, Hidden Path","descriptions":["A narrow path has been cleared through the clumps of sage bushes, tall grasses, untended wildflowers that grow abundantly here.  The tall somber trees of Wildulf Woods form a wall beyond a clearing to the north.  A small, cramped doorway leads back into the lodge."],"exits":[{"to":519,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":518,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":515,"exit":"go","move":"go small doorway"}]},
  {"id":518,"x":-800,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan Home, Seer's Circle","descriptions":["Within the densely-packed timberland sits a round, flat arena hemmed by a circle of hewn logs.  Two additional logs have been set at opposite sides of this circle, each adorned with talismans of feathers and beads affixed to the skulls of wolves.  Beneath them, leather strips dyed in bright colors dance and flutter in the soft breeze.  The arena itself is composed of hard-packed dirt which bears the scars of innumerable steps, slides and turns executed in some kind of precise, battle-inspired dance."],"exits":[{"to":517,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Mopeliar"]},
  {"id":519,"x":-780,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan Home, Secluded Clearing","descriptions":["A single aged willow tree stands in the center of this wide clearing, its drooping boughs sway and creak, reaching for the ground.  This ancient symbol of death and rebirth shelters an open-air shrine that has been erected at the base of the tree's gnarled trunk.  Small tufts of broad-leafed hosta plants surround the shrine.  Impenetrable walls of densely-packed trees and brush cut off any exit except to the south."],"exits":[{"to":517,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":520,"x":-720,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan, Wolverine Ward","descriptions":["Scratched into the dirt of the pathway is the remains of a circle with most of its line scuffed out.  Taken together with the disturbed area within the bounds, the purpose of the improvised wrestling ground is clear.  This open space between houses must often be used for such purposes, as there are a number of logs set upright near the edge of the road, ready to serve as seats for spectators."],"exits":[{"to":521,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":525,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":124,"exit":"go","move":"go winding path"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Wolverine Ward"]},
  {"id":521,"x":-680,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan, Wolverine Ward","descriptions":["A few boulders, left in place when the area was set up for housing, stand beside the road.  A few passersby have crudely hacked their names into the surface of the stones, sometimes with dates or other messages.  The houses stand well back from the roadway, most without fencing to separate them from their fellows."],"exits":[{"to":522,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":520,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":522,"x":-680,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan, Wolverine Ward","descriptions":["Sounds of metal being pounded come from within a shed attached to the side of a nearby house.  Wisps of smoke drift from the stovepipe jutting from the shed's roof, further evidence of metalwork being performed within.  Other homes nearby lack such sheds, but all are well-maintained."],"exits":[{"to":521,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":523,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":523,"x":-680,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan, Wolverine Ward","descriptions":["Hanging from a tree in the middle of the road is a colorful archery target, its surface much pierced from heavy use.  A number of scuffed-out lines show where the residents have used the roadway as an improvised archery range."],"exits":[{"to":522,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":524,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":524,"x":-700,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan, Wolverine Ward","descriptions":["Some of the nearby houses are surrounded by expanses of lawn but others have more working-class yards with small workbenches set up under the trees where residents can repair things while enjoying the open air.  All the homes, however, are sturdy and well-maintained against the weather."],"exits":[{"to":525,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":523,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":525,"x":-700,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Wolf Clan, Wolverine Ward","descriptions":["Children's bows and wooden weapons are strewn about one yard, obviously where an impromptu battle took place.  The cries of the children can be discerned in the distance, where they have run off to continue their play."],"exits":[{"to":524,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":520,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":526,"x":-620,"y":-580,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Steelpine Circle","descriptions":["Scattered along the dusty path are discarded weapon parts in various states of repair.  Ramshackle buildings crowd the pathway, their weathered boards and bricks giving an air of dilapadation to the area."],"exits":[{"to":531,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":527,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":457,"exit":"go","move":"go winding path"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":527,"x":-660,"y":-580,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Steelpine Circle","descriptions":["The ramshackle buildings huddle close to each other, as if seeking support and protection against the ravages of time and weather.  The almost uniform decrepit state they are in testifies to the fact that more than mutual support is needed to prevent the ravages of poverty and decay."],"exits":[{"to":526,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":528,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":528,"x":-660,"y":-560,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Steelpine Circle","descriptions":["Standing on a stout wooden platform, a metal pump head provides the inhabitants with fresh water.  The platform helps channel the runoff into a culvert that runs between the battered buildings of the area and disappears from sight.  The many tracks of bare feet through the dust testify to the heavy use the pump gets from the neighborhood."],"exits":[{"to":527,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":529,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":529,"x":-640,"y":-540,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Steelpine Circle","descriptions":["Crowded close together, the run-down buildings seem to lean against each other for support.  A few children's toys lie scattered in the dust of the main roadway, their cheerful colors a striking contrast with the general lack of color on the buildings."],"exits":[{"to":530,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":528,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":530,"x":-620,"y":-540,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Steelpine Circle","descriptions":["A trickle of muddy water crosses the dirt path here, its mucky waters filled with unidentifiable bits of slime and debris.  Wide tree trucks have been placed across the streamlet to provide a safe and sturdy crossing for the neighborhood's inhabitants."],"exits":[{"to":531,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":529,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":531,"x":-600,"y":-560,"z":0,"title":"Knife Clan, Steelpine Circle","descriptions":["Standing in the middle of a wide spot in the road is a octagonal message board covered in fading signs and notices.  Houses and shacks that are barely shelter line the dusty street, their walls and roofs barely able to keep out the weather."],"exits":[{"to":530,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":526,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":532,"x":-120,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Lake of Dreams, White Gladiolus Greenhouse","descriptions":["Nestled between Mycthengelde and the Lake of Dreams, a verdant hollow is encased in glass to form a greenhouse that is filled with frilled gladiolus blossoms.  Long tables placed at the center of the building are dressed in silk and ivy, each lit by rows of flickering candles.  Gentle ripples drift across the silvery surface of the nearby water, evidence of the stately procession of a pair of graceful white swans.","The deep, heady scent of gladiolus blossoms lingers in the night air, pervading a verdant lakeside hollow encased in glass and cloaked in darkness.  Rows of candles throw dancing shadows across long tables placed at the center of the building.  Flickering fireflies bob gently to and fro, their mesmerizing light reflected upon the placid surface of the nearby water."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["White Gladiolus Greenhouse","greenhouse"]},
  {"id":533,"x":-780,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Arnack's Tavern, Mud Pit","descriptions":["A large banner is suspended directly above the large, muddy pit that dominates the room.  Arranged in a semicircle around the pit, wooden benches are placed on platforms for better viewing."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":534,"exit":"go","move":"go curtained archway"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Mud pit"]},
  {"id":534,"x":-797,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Arnack's Tavern, Washroom","descriptions":["Faint, lingering traces of dried mud mar the otherwise pristine tile flooring.  Neatly arranged next to each other, a sturdy wooden counter, towel stand, and soap basin are placed near the entrance of the room."],"exits":[{"to":533,"exit":"go","move":"go curtained archway"},{"to":535,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden tub"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Arnack's Tavern, Washroom","washroom"]},
  {"id":535,"x":-797,"y":257,"z":0,"title":"Arnack's Tavern, Wooden Tub","descriptions":["Preventing the steaming, hot water from overflowing and spilling out of the tub, the tub's tall staves are carved with convenient handholds and footholds for bathers to exit easily."],"exits":[{"to":534,"exit":"climb","move":"climb tall staves"}],"color":"#0000FF"}
 ],
